&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a detail-oriented Payroll Tax and Compliance Analyst (based remotely in Ireland) to support payroll employment taxes, regulatory adherence, and mobility compliance across our APJ and EMEA regions. As a fast-growing tech company, our workforce is highly mobile. Working closely with internal stakeholders and external tax/payroll advisors, you will help ensure accurate tax withholding, social security application, and statutory compliance across multiple jurisdictions. Reporting to the Director, Global Payroll, you will execute compliance workflows, flag potential risks, and support seamless payroll operations for a dynamic, global team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tax Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate recurring payroll tax compliance, statutory filings, and general ledger reconciliations across APJ and EMEA (covering Ireland, UK, Sweden, Spain, France, Poland, Germany, Estonia, Belgium, Australia, India, Singapore, Japan, and Hong Kong) in partnership with local payroll vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobility Tracking:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor employee movement, international business travel, and cross-border transfers to ensure timely and accurate payroll tax withholding and shadow payroll reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nexus Assessment: &lt;/strong&gt;Track remote worker locations and cross-border travel data, flagging potential corporate tax footprint or Permanent Establishment (PE) triggers to Corporate Tax and Legal teams for review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Social Security:&lt;/strong&gt; Administer local social security contributions and coordinate Certificates of Coverage (A1 forms and bilateral totalisation agreements) for internationally mobile employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Research:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor upcoming tax law changes, statutory rate updates, and local filing requirements across active jurisdictions, updating internal compliance calendars and SOPs accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as a day-to-day operational contact for local payroll partners, external tax advisors, and auditors, preparing supporting schedules and resolving routine tax authority queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Year-End Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Execute and track country-specific year-end tax reporting processes across APJ and EMEA, ensuring timely statutory submissions and employee tax certificate distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify opportunities to streamline workflows and improve data accuracy for mobile employee tax adjustments and compliance tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: 3+ years of multi-country payroll, payroll tax, or global mobility compliance experience, ideally within a fast-paced technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Geographic Scope: Working knowledge of EMEA and/or APJ statutory payroll taxes, filings, and social security frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobility Expertise: Solid understanding of cross-border employee taxation, shadow payroll concepts, trailing liabilities, and remote work compliance considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Skills: Proficiency with global payroll and HRIS platforms (e.g., Workday, Deel) and strong spreadsheet/data reconciliation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: Strong ability to document complex statutory requirements into clear standard operating procedures (SOPs) and communicate tax updates effectively to employees and internal teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with payroll compliance in one or more of our key jurisdictions (Ireland, UK, Sweden, Spain, France, Poland, Germany, Estonia, Australia, India, Singapore, Japan, Hong Kong).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IPASS qualification, Certified Payroll Professional (CPP), or equivalent international payroll/tax certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payroll tax withholding and reporting for equity compensation (RSUs, ESPPs, stock options) across multiple tax jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;This role will be remote, and based in Ireland.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize connection and opportunities to build relationships with our customers and each other. For this role, approximately 5% travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Twilio offers many benefits, including competitive pay, generous time off, ample parental and wellness leave, healthcare, a retirement savings program, and much more. Offerings vary by location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
