&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is needed to design, build, and optimize Twilio&#39;s next-generation unified data platforms and services to power strategic, data-driven business decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior technical leader on our Enterprise Data Engineering team, you will drive a massive, highly visible transformation to unify disparate data lakes into a single, high-performance platform. By combining classic dimensional modeling with cutting-edge AI, you will accelerate data delivery at an immense scale. This is your chance to solve complex architectural challenges, mentor rising talent, and directly influence Twilio’s strategic direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and scale high-performance data platforms to unify acquired data lakes, improving delivery speed by leveraging AI-driven workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design robust ETL pipelines and data integration frameworks using Spark, dbt, and AWS to support rapidly growing enterprise data needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish rigorous data modeling standards (Dimensional, Medallion) and implement full-stack observability to ensure data trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor peer engineers, promoting technical excellence and living our We &amp;gt; Me value through active collaboration with architects and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
