&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fin.ai/&quot;&gt;Fin&lt;/a&gt;, now part of Salesforce, is on a mission to help businesses provide perfect customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our AI Agent Fin is the highest-performing AI Customer Agent on the market today, enabling businesses to deliver impeccable, always-on customer support across the customer journey, from service, to sales, to ecommerce. Powered by our own AI models, Fin resolves complex customer issues end-to-end across every channel, with minimal set-up and integration. Fin can also be combined with our natively integrated Intercom help desk, giving modern support teams one single system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together with Salesforce, the #1 AI CRM, where humans with agents drive customer success, we&#39;re building the future of customer experience. Here, ambition meets action. Tech meets trust. And innovation isn&#39;t a buzzword, it&#39;s a way of life. The world of work as we know it is changing, and we&#39;re looking for Trailblazers who are passionate about bettering business and the world through AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to level up your career at the company leading workforce transformation in the agentic era? You&#39;re in the right place. Agentforce is the future of AI, and you are the future of Salesforce.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s the opportunity?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for Senior+ AI Infrastructure Engineers with deep GPU and low-level performance expertise to make Fin&#39;s models train faster and serve more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fin is an AI company that builds from the GPU all the way up to a user agent that resolves millions of customer service queries a month. Our AI Infrastructure team built the training pipelines and runs the inference for custom models like Fin Apex, which outperforms frontier models in customer service tasks at a fraction of the cost.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For someone coming from CUDA, HIP, Triton or low-level performance engineering, this role is a chance to apply that expertise across training and inference. You&#39;ll profile the stack, find where GPU time and memory bandwidth are being lost, then tune or write the kernels that win it back. We&#39;ve worked on projects from custom attention methods to model integrations in vLLM. Your improvements land directly in production as faster training, higher inference throughput and lower latency for millions of conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll also have room to work above the kernel layer. You&#39;ll collaborate with engineers and ML scientists across training and serving, see how low-level decisions affect the whole system, and help shape Fin&#39;s longer-term GPU and performance architecture. Hardware and performance is your home base, but you&#39;ll have the opportunity to build expertise in model training and in high-availability, high-efficiency inference too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior AI Infrastructure Engineer focused on GPU performance, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve accelerator utilisation and throughput for distributed training of large transformer models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive down inference latency and cost through work like quantisation, speculative decoding and integration with serving engines such as vLLM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, write and tune custom accelerator kernels (CUDA, Triton, HIP or similar), such as attention variants, fused operators and low-precision paths, and land them in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug hard numerical and performance problems wherever they live, including inside third-party GPU libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build profiling, benchmarking and correctness tooling that makes performance work faster and safer for the whole team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with ML scientists early, so the performance cost of a model design is known before it&#39;s trained or served, and help bring new methods to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape Fin&#39;s longer-term GPU, cluster and performance architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play an active role in hiring, mentoring and developing other engineers, and raise the bar for technical standards and operational excellence across Fin&#39;s AI platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profile we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These are indicative, not hard requirements. You&#39;re likely a great fit if:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of experience in software engineering, with a strong track record of shipping high-quality, performance-critical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You hold a degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering or a related field, or have equivalent experience with very strong fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have hands-on experience writing and optimising ML accelerator kernels, for example in CUDA, Triton or HIP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how GPUs and other ML accelerators work under the hood: memory hierarchy, matrix units, how work is parallelised and scheduled on the hardware, and what bounds a kernel by compute, memory or communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re fluent with profiling tools such as Nsight Systems, Nsight Compute or the PyTorch profiler, and can turn a trace into a concrete fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable working in production environments at meaningful scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly, can explain complex technical topics to different audiences, and enjoy close collaboration with both engineers and non-engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take pride in strong technical fundamentals, love learning, and are keen to grow beyond the kernel layer into training and serving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have deep knowledge of at least one programming language (for example Python, Ruby, Java, Go, C++ etc.). Specific language experience is less important than your ability to write clean, reliable code and learn new stacks quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus skills &amp;amp; attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;None of these are required, but they&#39;re nice to have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of transformer internals, and of how training and inference scale across many GPUs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and PyTorch, and comfort in C++ when the work calls for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with kernel libraries and DSLs such as CUTLASS/CuTe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making models run in FP8, FP4 or other reduced-precision formats without losing accuracy, in training or inference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with inference engines such as vLLM, SGLang or TensorRT-LLM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with collective communication (e.g. NCCL, RCCL) and multi-node performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience below the framework layer, such as compiler development, hardware or chip design, or contributing to the internals of PyTorch, JAX or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at AI-native companies that train and/or run inference for their own models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running training or inference workloads on Kubernetes, and on AWS or another major cloud provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated passion for performance work through open source, personal projects, talks or published writing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unleash Your Potential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
