&lt;h1&gt;About the role&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a curious, thorough and commercially minded CRO Specialist to join our CX &amp;amp; CRO Management team under Ecommerce Operations. Your starting question will be: “What is stopping someone from buying today?” Working with a high degree of autonomy, you will independently identify conversion issues and improvement opportunities across a portfolio of ecommerce retailers, using judgement to determine the appropriate depth of investigation and engaging the teams responsible for delivering changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines independent day-to-day monitoring with deep-dive analysis across complex and varied business questions. You will balance timely action on emerging issues with a prioritised programme of short- and medium-term improvements, receiving general direction on new priorities rather than detailed oversight of day-to-day work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using GA4, Shopify Analytics, ESW’s internal BI data and behavioural tools, you will explore international shopper behaviour across fashion, luxury, consumer goods and digital goods. You will turn evidence into practical recommendations for Customer Success Managers and retailer partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Conversion monitoring and ownership&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently monitor conversion and funnel progression by retailer, geography, device and traffic source, using consistent metric definitions and meaningful comparisons to identify where attention is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detect unusual changes, pinpoint the affected funnel stage and independently assess tracking and data quality before investigating shopper behaviour. Exercise judgement to determine the appropriate action within agreed operating practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the triage of conversion losses, coordinate cross-functional investigation and track recovery with minimal day-to-day supervision. Maintain accountability for performance follow-up while technical and operational teams own implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Deep-dive analysis and conversion improvements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently combine funnel data, behavioural evidence and commercial context to understand why shoppers abandon their journey, evaluating alternative explanations before reaching a conclusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse complex and varied patterns across markets, brand categories and traffic profiles, accounting for shopper intent, localisation and local expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop evidence-based hypotheses and independently prioritise improvements by conversion impact, commercial value, effort and confidence. Quantify opportunities where the evidence supports it and recommend the appropriate course of action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend changes and A/B tests for CX roadmaps, using professional judgement to shape the analysis and test approach. Evaluate outcomes against suitable baselines, accounting for traffic shifts, seasonality and data limitations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Communication and ways of working&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively share concise performance updates, findings and recommendations with Customer Success Managers and retailer partners, tailoring the level of detail to the audience and confidently explaining the rationale behind recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage priorities across the assigned retailer portfolio, escalating material risks or dependencies when appropriate. Build stakeholder alignment and share reusable learnings that contribute to broader team goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work autonomously with data and technical teams to resolve access, tracking gaps and reporting needs. Develop AI-assisted workflows to reduce repetitive work, validating outputs before use and sharing effective practices with the wider team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in &lt;strong&gt;ecommerce analytics, digital analytics, conversion rate optimisation or a similar data-focused role&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An investigative mindset and the ability to work fully independently, with the rigour to evaluate identifiable factors, test alternative explanations and determine an appropriate course of action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on GA4 expertise in ecommerce funnels and segmentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret international shopper behaviour in the context of local markets, brand positioning and acquisition channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial judgement to balance potential value, investigation depth and timely action, making sound decisions with minimal day-to-day instruction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear writing and presentation skills for both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative and accountable approach to independently managing work across retailers, following through on agreed actions and providing informal guidance or mentoring to junior colleagues when appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Shopify Analytics, BI platforms and behavioural analytics tools. Able to apply professional knowledge creatively to solve unfamiliar problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel or Google Sheets and reporting skills, with experience in AI-assisted analysis or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound understanding of data quality, experiment evaluation and attribution limits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About ESW&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our purpose is simple: to create moments that matter between people and the brands they cherish. We enable brands to expand their global reach, facilitating simple and seamless ecommerce experiences for consumers worldwide. Through our integration solutions, we deliver a complete international checkout experience, including local duties, taxes, fulfilment, delivery management, and global returns and payment processing capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guided by our values—Own It, Champion Simplicity, Win as One, and Debate then Commit—we strive to foster innovation, accountability, and teamwork, creating solutions that inspire trust and drive impactful results.&lt;/p&gt;
