&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Smartling is an AI-native translation platform that’s redefining how the world’s biggest brands go global, ranked &lt;strong&gt;#3 on Fast Company’s Most Innovative Companies&lt;/strong&gt; list. We’re growing rapidly at scale and are backed by Vitruvian Partners, a global technology-focused investment firm. While most companies are still figuring out how to use AI, we’ve spent years building it into the core of our platform, and we’re just getting started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Localisation Project Manager (Localisation Operations Specialist) based in Ireland or the UK to join our Managed Services team. In this role, you&#39;ll own the end-to-end localisation lifecycle for a portfolio of enterprise clients, serving as both their operational point of contact and a key contributor to how our team delivers value. This is a role for someone who brings real localisation experience, thrives in a fast-paced, remote-first environment, and is energized by the challenge of balancing operational precision with strong client relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as your clients&#39; embedded localisation operations expert, serving as the primary operational point of contact and trusted advisor for assigned accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster strong stakeholder relationships, navigate competing priorities, and coordinate cross-functional teams to ensure the successful execution and continuous improvement of clients&#39; localization programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and optimize localisation processes within Smartling’s platform and client-preferred project management and content management tools, overseeing the end-to-end job lifecycle and tailoring configurations to each client’s unique requirements, including effective use of AI tooling where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve problems both independently and collaboratively, bringing a solutions-first mindset to client challenges and internal roadblocks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively drive operational excellence by identifying and implementing process improvements, documenting best practices, and leveraging automation and AI-enabled solutions to streamline workflows, enhance scalability, and improve team efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2-3 years of experience in localisation or translation project management, ideally within a managed services or agency environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of localisation file formats, content types, and CAT/TMS tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong client management skills: comfortable leading calls, navigating difficult conversations, and representing the team externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with project management and reporting tools (e.g., Jira, Asana, Google Sheets, Looker, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating with cross-functional teams across engineering, QA, and vendor management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and time management skills, with sharp attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred but not required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Smartling or other TMS platforms (such as Phrase, XTM, or MemoQ)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise or SaaS clients in an operational or customer-facing role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency or working proficiency in a second language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in language, technology, or global content strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accountable. &lt;/strong&gt;You take full ownership of your accounts, addressing issues promptly and documenting root causes and preventative actions for future improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer-Focused. &lt;/strong&gt;You understand that client deadlines and requirements are real business commitments and consistently approach them with urgency, accountability, and care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptable. &lt;/strong&gt;You adjust effectively to changing scope, priorities, and unexpected client inputs without losing focus or execution quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communicative. &lt;/strong&gt;You proactively stay ahead of client needs by sharing status updates, surfacing risks early, and contributing insights, guidance, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process-Driven. &lt;/strong&gt;You adhere to established processes while actively identifying opportunities to improve efficiency and consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will Enjoy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Freedom 🏡- we are remote-first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth - an opportunity to learn and advance your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wealth 💰 - we offer a competitive salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
