&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Airbnb Hotels team is a fun, fast-growing group leading Airbnb’s expansion into the hotel sector. Operating with an entrepreneurial spirit, this team combines the simplicity, product excellence and guest-centred ethos that define Airbnb. Our mission is to deliver the smoothest, most intuitive hotel booking experience for guests, while helping hotel partners easily drive incremental bookings so they can focus on delivering the best hospitality. The ultimate aim is to help more people discover high-quality hotels, creating value for guests and our hotel partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build a global team. Open doors no one at Airbnb has opened yet.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb Hotels is one of the most exciting growth stories in travel, and we’re only getting started. As Manager, Key Accounts, you will build and lead a brand new, globally distributed team of Enterprise Account Managers. Together you will win and onboard high-value, above-property hotel groups with hundreds of hotels across multiple continents.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who brings:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven leadership of a key, strategic or enterprise accounts team&lt;/strong&gt;, ideally globally distributed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A network and reputation in travel and hospitality&lt;/strong&gt;, ideally hotels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real negotiation experience &lt;/strong&gt;with high-value partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A builder’s mindset,&lt;/strong&gt; with a track record of creating teams, playbooks and processes where none existed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong cross-functional influence&lt;/strong&gt; across a matrix organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end partner management at hotel headquarter and regional office level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mutual account plans that drive supply and strategic relationship value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The global Key Accounts strategy, in line with the Enterprise Team playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear mandate to consistently exceed quarterly business KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;World-class account management practices, operational excellence and partner satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The voice of Key Accounts within Hotels leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, growth-oriented team that you mentor and motivate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position reports to the Global Head, Hotel Enterprise and Connectivity Partnerships, and offers a unique opportunity to shape Airbnb’s growth in the hotel market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead a brand new team&lt;/strong&gt; in a business that only launched this year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the Key Accounts playbook&lt;/strong&gt; from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the relationships,&lt;/strong&gt; the targets and the strategy for a global segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with a leadership team that is moving fast &lt;/strong&gt;and backing this business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a distributed team of Enterprise Account Managers, supporting them on partner management and new business development for supply acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the team’s quarterly revenue, supply acquisition and OKR targets, and ensure they are met and exceeded&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take partners from first conversation through negotiation, signed deal and onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute the Key Accounts playbook in line with global strategy, working closely with Hotel functional teams across regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and grow relationships with multi-national hotel groups, acting as an escalation option for your team where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the operational rhythm for the team: establish and track KPIs, analyse growth and key metrics to identify trends, surface new business opportunities, and resolve business challenges with urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Hotels field team in achieving their goals through well-designed field-level action plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product, Technical Support, Connectivity, RevOps and Hotels Cross-Functional Leadership to drive feature adoption and business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Airbnb at industry and partner events, and organise internal partner events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold regular team meetings, 1:1s, and performance and development reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organise team business gatherings, quarterly kick-offs and team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must-haves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of professional experience and at least 8+ years in sales or account management roles in travel, hospitality or e-commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience managing and leading high-performing teams, with a proven track record of meeting and exceeding goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a globally distributed team and driving solutions to improve supply acquisition and revenue goals, ideally across international markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with, or deep knowledge of, major hotel groups across the global hospitality landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset developed from experience having launched companies, teams or significant initiatives where resources, processes and capabilities had to be created, not handed to you or followed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of preparing and executing complex negotiations with high-value partner organisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly motivated team builder with the ability to coach and mentor account managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop a strategy, communicate it clearly, and secure buy-in and support to execute against quarterly goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills to identify opportunities, operationalise execution with regional teams, and drive business results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence senior executives, both within regional Airbnb leadership and within partner leadership teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work within a matrix, solve problems, and influence cross-functional and cross-regional teams, with strong stakeholder management across Marketing, Legal, FP&amp;amp;A, Payments, Product, regional field teams, and Enterprise and Connectivity teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel globally up to 60% of the time as needed to meet team members and engage with partners and customers at industry events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the hospitality technology space, including familiarity with OTAs and hotel distribution (strongly preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and driving channel sales and marketing initiatives with global partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with tools such as CRM tools (Salesforce), project management tools (Asana, Airtable), and business intelligence tools (Tableau, Looker, Claude)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French or another major European language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Ireland Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€102.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€128.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two Hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 4 million Hosts who have welcomed more than 1 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, Hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Quality Lead for Rest of World (ROW) supports Airbnb&#39;s non-English Community Support partner network, covering the EMEA and CJK (Chinese, Japanese, Korean) language Volume Tiers. This lead oversees the day-to-day quality operation across multiple BPO partners and service lines, across ROW-language agents globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an execution and leadership role. The Quality Lead is responsible for making the quality program work on the ground: ensuring partner QA teams are calibrated and accountable, translating quality standards into partner behavior, surfacing performance trends early, and driving the actions that close gaps. This Lead directly manages and leads the EMEA and CJK Quality Partner Leads, who work directly with partners to manage and drive performance, and also works directly with Quality Leaders across the different partners supporting ROW. This Lead will direct the focus and energy of these resources toward what matters, remove blockers, help address areas of opportunity, and hold the overall ROW quality program to a consistent standard across regions, languages and time zones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROW Quality Program Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the day-to-day execution of the ROW quality program across all in-scope Volume Tier service lines and all EMEA and CJK partner sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure weekly QA evaluation targets are met across all sites, languages and service lines; monitor evaluation completeness, calibration accuracy, and coaching activity within the ROW portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the weekly QA performance reporting cadence, ensuring partner QA teams and Partner Operations Managers receive timely, accurate, and actionable quality data each week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop the EMEA and CJK Quality Partner Leads: set priorities, align regional approaches, and ensure consistent standards and ways of working across both regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Network Governance &amp;amp; Accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold ROW partner QA teams accountable to the Performance Scorecard results: Agent Saturation Targets, Evaluation Completeness, Calibration Accuracy, Coaching Effectiveness, Actionable Insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain regular engagement with Partner Quality teams: weekly alignment cadences and alignment on monthly business review results and actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate partner performance gaps and establish documented action plans where warranted; escalate to Sr. Leadership for situations that require it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the New Site Onboarding process for any new ROW partner sites that come online, ensuring they are calibrated to ROW quality standards before they scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calibration &amp;amp; Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct calibration sessions across EMEA and CJK partner sites; ensure calibration rigor so that ROW quality is measured consistently regardless of partner, language or geography.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure calibration of non-English evaluations is aligned to global standards, including cross-language and cross-region consistency with Global English where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive QA alignment across Quality and Delivery teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insights, NPS Correlation &amp;amp; the AQS North Star&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee NPS Detractor Analysis Insights to identify drivers of dissatisfaction, including language- and market-specific drivers; work with Delivery, Training, and other stakeholders to address areas of opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Correlate quality results to operational outcomes and KPIs; place quality focus and emphasis accordingly, based on operational measures that require attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure ROW quality insights are integrated into the weekly partner performance narrative: when scores drop week-over-week, understand drivers and root cause, and be able to explain them in weekly reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the ROW Training team on critical initiatives, such as Training Flight Simulator and AirReady; Quality&#39;s role is to ensure training artifacts related to Quality are aligned to our Lead With Hospitality framework, including localization for EMEA and CJK markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate as the ROW quality voice in cross-functional working groups, where quality findings have direct implications for process or content change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface patterns from ROW evaluations that signal policy gaps, workflow failures, or product issues — not just agent-level coaching opportunities. When the same investigation error appears across three different partner sites in the same week, that is a systemic issue that belongs in OneTrack, not a coaching note.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Operational Cadences&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the ROW contribution to the global Quality reporting framework: weekly KPI data by site and language (NPS, Reopen Rate, AQS, 0–60, Throughput) submitted accurately and on time as part of the automated reporting rollout, replacing the current manual slide validation process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure ROW partner sites are submitting their own KPI narratives with substance — not high-level summaries or incorrect figures. The Quality Partner Lead&#39;s job is to verify narrative quality, not just numbers; this role&#39;s job is to ensure that standard is held across all ROW partner networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the ROW calendar of quality touchpoints: weekly partner performance reviews, monthly calibration sessions, monthly partner business reviews, and quarterly COPC-style partner capability assessments — and ensure the Quality Partner Lead team is prepared and present for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in Community/Customer Support Quality, Operations, or a related field, with direct experience managing QA programs across BPO or partner networks at meaningful scale (1,000+ agents across multiple sites).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of direct people management experience — specifically managing QA Leads or Quality Partner Leads who themselves have partner oversight responsibilities, not just individual QIAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading quality across multiple regions and languages, including managing leaders in different geographies and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience driving partner BPO accountability: running calibration sessions, managing partner QA scorecards, writing and executing improvement plans, and holding BPO QA managers to performance standards in a governance context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of COPC methodology; able to apply COPC evaluation standards, sampling requirements, and calibration governance in a live multi-partner operational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills: able to read weekly QA performance data, diagnose root causes behind score movements (tenure mix, calibration drift, form changes, workflow updates), and translate that diagnosis into a clear narrative for Delivery and partner leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with QA tooling platforms — Observe.AI, NICE QC, or equivalent — including form design, calibration management, and partner site onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication in English; able to write a sharp partner performance email, run a productive calibration session across time zones, and present quality findings to senior Delivery stakeholders with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a BPO or multi-site QA role, either in-house at a BPO or as a client-side quality manager managing multiple BPO partners simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional proficiency in one or more EMEA or CJK languages, or experience quality-managing non-English support operations through calibration and localization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Airbnb&#39;s Volume Tier service lines (R1, R2, R3, DSS, S&amp;amp;E, DMHS) or equivalent hospitality/travel platform support programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the Lead With Hospitality (LWH) framework, COPC-aligned behavioral QA rubrics, or equivalent structured quality frameworks with fatal-scoring models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Six Sigma Green Belt or equivalent structured problem-solving background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with analytics teams on QA-to-NPS or QA-to-CSAT correlation analysis; experience using AQS (Ambassador Quality Score) or equivalent composite agent performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cross-functional quality improvement programs — investigation skills initiatives, coaching ambassador programs, agent messaging tone efforts — and experience coordinating quality&#39;s role in multi-team rollouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
