&lt;p&gt;Toast creates technology to help restaurants and local businesses succeed in a digital world, helping business owners operate, increase sales, engage customers, and keep employees happy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Infrastructure Engineering team’s mission is to provide cloud native infrastructure, automation and tools that enable teams across Toast to deliver products in a safe, secure and agile manner, with minimal operational dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Infrastructure Engineer, you will be responsible for platform architecture and providing the automation and implementation for landing zones as well as network and security infrastructure for new AWS regions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life (Responsibilities)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within a Scrum team to create, document and support various infrastructure as code modules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, document and support various tools and services used in order to support continuous integration, continuous delivery and continuous deployment of highly available infrastructure in various environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use your familiarity with DevOps methodologies and practices to foster a culture of quality while facilitating developer velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create tools to help our developers move their infrastructure from a monolithic repo to individual service repos for use with our IDP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You believe internal tools deserve unit tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example with code standards and design; help implement these across the scrum team’s products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support developers within the organisation on using and extending of IaC tooling and support systems using DevOps methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need to thrive (Requirements)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 6+ years of software engineering experience, specialising in DevOps/Infrastructure/Platform engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with object orientated programming is a &lt;strong&gt;MUST&lt;/strong&gt; for this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must have hands on experience with writing Terraform Providers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with at least one public cloud computing offering such as AWS, GCP or Azure infrastructure SDKs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with Infrastructure-as-Code framework internals &amp;amp; SDKs (Terraform providers, Ansible modules &amp;amp; plugins, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining large-scale infrastructure, including both production and nonproduction workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the continuous integration, deployment, and delivery of Cloud Infrastructure at scale for technology teams of hundreds of developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A desire to build a diverse team that wins together and prioritises customer success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading the build and scale of critical platform features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will help you stand out (Nonessential Skills/Nice to Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure/experience using AI tools such as Claude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
