&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P25788_3538423&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Below is the annual On Target Compensation (OTE) range for candidates located in Ireland. Your actual OTE, which is inclusive of base salary and incentive compensation, will depend on factors such as your skills, qualifications, experience, and work location. In addition, Okta offers equity (where applicable) and comprehensive healthcare coverage and financial benefits including paid time off and parental leave in accordance with our applicable plans and policies. To learn more about our Total Rewards program please visit: https://rewards.okta.com/irl.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The OTE range for this position for candidates located in Ireland is between:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€196.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€264.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a strategic, data-driven, and highly resourceful &lt;strong&gt;EMEA Digital Media Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to own regional digital acquisition and paid media strategy across priority EMEA markets, including UKI, France, Germany, the Netherlands, and other key growth regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;manager-level individual contributor role&lt;/strong&gt; with significant autonomy and regional ownership. You will translate global marketing strategy into an EMEA digital media plan, determine how investment should be deployed across markets and channels, and continuously optimize toward qualified demand, pipeline, and revenue outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires more than strong platform execution. We are looking for someone who can develop a clear regional point of view, identify where performance is strong or weak, recommend where investment should shift, and influence senior regional and global stakeholders with data-backed recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a T-shaped digital leader who operates at the intersection of paid media, marketing technology, analytics, buyer behavior, and localization. You will use AI and automation to increase speed and scale while ensuring regional programs remain relevant to the local market and connected to measurable business outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own EMEA Digital Media Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and lead the regional paid media strategy across priority EMEA markets, translating global priorities into market-specific investment, audience, channel, and activation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage Regional Investment &amp;amp; Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Own regional paid media budgets and recommend shifts across geographies, channels, campaigns, and buyer motions based on performance, pipeline contribution, and market opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Full-Funnel Digital Acquisition:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and optimize integrated programs across Paid Search, Paid Social, Programmatic Display, retargeting, content syndication, and ABM/ABX motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Regional Performance Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Move beyond platform metrics to evaluate inquiry quality, qualified demand, opportunity creation, pipeline progression, and revenue impact, identifying where demand is—and is not—progressing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop a Regional Point of View:&lt;/strong&gt; Surface trends and performance insights across EMEA and proactively recommend changes to targeting, media mix, creative, offers, and investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead AI &amp;amp; Workflow Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and scale practical uses of generative AI and automation across localization, audience development, creative testing, campaign operations, analysis, and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence Cross-Functional Stakeholders:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the senior digital media partner to EMEA Field Marketing, Global Demand Generation, Product Marketing, Marketing Operations, Sales Development, and global media teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advance Signal-Based Marketing:&lt;/strong&gt; Incorporate intent, engagement, account, web, and CRM signals into media targeting and activation to improve buyer progression and investment efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Measurement &amp;amp; Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Marketing Operations and Analytics to strengthen conversion tracking, offline signal feedback, attribution, and platform optimization toward qualified business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Localization &amp;amp; Vendor Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage regional agencies and partners, ensuring localized campaigns achieve both cultural relevance and performance objectives while maintaining global brand standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish a regional test-and-learn roadmap across audiences, creative, channels, bidding strategies, and emerging media opportunities, translating results into scalable recommendations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years of experience in digital media, digital acquisition, or demand generation, ideally within a high-growth B2B technology or enterprise SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated success managing digital programs across multiple European markets and navigating meaningful differences in buyer behavior, media ecosystems, language, and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic + Hands-On Capability:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to move comfortably between setting media strategy, analyzing performance, making investment recommendations, and going directly into platforms when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B2B Enterprise SaaS Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong understanding of complex enterprise buying cycles and how paid media contributes across awareness, demand capture, pipeline creation, and opportunity progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment Judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing meaningful media budgets and making data-backed decisions about where to scale, reduce, or redirect investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Rigor:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced ability to translate complex performance data into a clear business story, recommendation, and action. Experience with platforms such as Tableau or Looker, Salesforce, Marketo, and web analytics tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paid Media Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep proficiency across major paid media platforms and acquisition strategies, including Google Ads, LinkedIn, programmatic media, audience targeting, bidding, measurement, and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Marketing Technology Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong interest in using AI, automation, and emerging marketing technology to increase effectiveness, speed, and scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication &amp;amp; Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to synthesize complex inputs into concise recommendations and confidently influence stakeholders across global and regional organizations without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Builder Mentality:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to operate through ambiguity, identify gaps, build better processes, and drive work forward independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Linguistic &amp;amp; Cultural Literacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in English and strong understanding of localization across EMEA markets; fluency in another major European language is highly advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; A strong team orientation and willingness to contribute beyond immediate scope when needed to drive shared regional and global outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(P10258_3505172)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Below is the annual salary range for candidates located in Ireland. Your actual salary will depend on factors such as your skills, qualifications, and experience. In addition, Okta offers equity (where applicable), bonus, and comprehensive healthcare coverage and financial benefits including paid time off and parental leave in accordance with our applicable plans and policies. To learn more about our Total Rewards program, please visit: https://rewards.okta.com/irl.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base salary range for this position for candidates located in Ireland is between:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€72.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€99.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Based in our &lt;strong&gt;Dublin, Ireland&lt;/strong&gt; office and reporting directly to the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Global Security &amp;amp; Safety&lt;/strong&gt;, the Global Health &amp;amp; Safety Manager will own the design, execution, governance, and continuous enhancement of Okta’s global health, safety, and occupational wellness framework.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While anchored in Dublin, this is a &lt;strong&gt;broad, truly global leadership role&lt;/strong&gt;. Because Okta operates dynamic, distributed workplaces across multiple international jurisdictions, the Global Health &amp;amp; Safety Manager will scale operations by directing an extensive network of specialized third-party vendors, global EHS consultants, and local practitioners. In addition to overarching workplace safety, this leader serves as the global program owner for Okta’s &lt;strong&gt;Workers’ Compensation and Occupational Injury/Illness Claims Management&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. 3rd-Party Vendor Management &amp;amp; Global Partner Ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the principal manager and strategic owner of Okta’s global health and safety vendor ecosystem, including multinational EHS environmental/safety consulting firms, localized safety practitioners, and specialized service partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Statements of Work (SOWs), key performance indicators (KPIs), and service level agreements (SLAs) for external EHS partners supporting regional risk assessments, statutory testing, and compliance filings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor procurement, contract evaluations, invoicing, and quarterly business reviews (QBRs) to ensure cost-efficiency, technical rigor, and consistent service delivery across all global locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct external partners in conducting localized site inspections, air quality monitoring, industrial hygiene assessments, and acoustic/lighting studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Global Workers&#39; Compensation &amp;amp; Claims Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the single point of contact and global program manager for Okta’s Workers’ Compensation, Employers&#39; Liability, and occupational injury/illness programs across all global jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with People Operations (HR), Risk Management/Treasury, legal counsel, insurance brokers, and Third-Party Claims Administrators (TPAs) to oversee claim lifecycles, reserve tracking, and settlements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and manage a global &lt;strong&gt;Return-to-Work (RTW)&lt;/strong&gt; and modified-duty framework to support injured or ill employees and safely reduce lost time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular claims audits, review carrier loss-run reports, identify global workplace injury trends, and execute root-cause mitigation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory reporting compliance across regions (e.g., Irish Health and Safety Authority [HSA] statutory notifications, US OSHA 300 logs, and relevant EMEA/APAC incident reporting requirements).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Global Health &amp;amp; Safety Governance &amp;amp; Statutory Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate, maintain, and enforce Okta’s global Health &amp;amp; Safety standard operating procedures (SOPs), workplace safety manuals, and corporate safety policies across all regional hubs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor multi-jurisdictional compliance across all regions (e.g., Irish Safety, Health and Welfare at Work Act, EU Workplace Directives, UK HSE regulations, US OSHA standards, and APAC regional health codes), leveraging specialized regional legal and consulting partners where necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee site-level risk assessments (General Risk Assessments, Fire Risk Assessments, Display Screen Equipment/DSE assessments) and track all corrective actions to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Okta’s primary liaison for statutory safety authorities, labor inspectorates, municipal fire services, and external compliance auditors worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Global Ergonomics &amp;amp; Preventive Wellness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct Okta’s Global Ergonomics Program across both physical corporate offices and our distributed, remote-first workforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with external ergonomic evaluation platforms, specialized ergonomic physical therapists/evaluators, and internal workplace experience teams to review complex cases and reasonable accommodation requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the ergonomic evaluation workflow, self-assessment software adoption, and equipment reimbursement guidelines in alignment with corporate policy and regional procurement structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Emergency Preparedness, GSOC Coordination &amp;amp; Safety Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead incident investigation workflows for global safety incidents, significant near-misses, and occupational health concerns; determine root causes and institute corrective and preventive actions (CAPA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Okta&#39;s Global Security Operations Center (GSOC), Physical Security, and Workplace Experience teams to ensure rapid incident escalation and crisis coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize life safety programs globally, including local Emergency Wardens, First Aiders, evacuation drills, automated external defibrillator (AED) maintenance, and emergency supply readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, track, and report on global safety metrics (such as Lost Time Injury Frequency Rates [LTIFR], Total Recordable Incident Rates [TRIR], ergonomics SLA closures, and vendor performance).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 6+ years of progressive professional experience leading environmental health, safety, and occupational wellness programs within multinational enterprise or fast-paced technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Scope:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated experience managing health and safety programs across multi-site global portfolios spanning EMEA, the Americas, and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor &amp;amp; Partner Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of managing global EHS third-party vendors, specialized consulting firms, and outsourced safety service providers to scale global coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workers&#39; Compensation &amp;amp; Claims:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong, direct experience managing global or multi-regional workers&#39; compensation programs, employer liability claims, TPAs, and structured Return-to-Work (RTW) processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid understanding of Irish Health and Safety Authority (HSA) statutory requirements and EU Health &amp;amp; Safety Directives, paired with the capability to oversee international compliance frameworks (e.g., US OSHA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Certifications &amp;amp; Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Occupational Health &amp;amp; Safety, Environmental Science, Risk Management, or related field (or equivalent practical experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognized professional health and safety certification (e.g., NEBOSH Diploma/Certificate, GradIOSH / CMIOSH, CSP, or recognized equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to partner effectively across People/HR, Workplace/Real Estate, Physical Security/GSOC, Legal, and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and scaling remote/hybrid ergonomic programs and digital ergonomics assessment platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating health and safety workflows with 24/7 Global Security Operations Centers (GSOC) and enterprise crisis management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing casualty insurance broker reviews and global risk management underwriting surveys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location &amp;amp; Working Arrangement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Office:&lt;/strong&gt; Dublin, Ireland.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Model:&lt;/strong&gt; Hybrid (combining scheduled on-site collaboration at our Dublin office with remote flexibility, while accommodating global time zone collaboration across EMEA, AMER, and APAC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Occasional international and regional travel (approx. 10–15%) to regional hubs, major global offices, and partner sites as operational needs dictate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(P10919_3557647)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
