&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Okta is looking for a Recruiting Operations Specialist to join our EMEA Recruiting team, based in our Dublin hub.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible role at the heart of how candidates experience Okta. Embedded within our wider People team, you’ll work closely with Recruiters, Workplace, Executive Assistants and Business Leaders to create memorable candidate experiences while ensuring the operational work behind our hiring runs seamlessly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be a key partner to our recruiters and often one of the first faces of Okta for candidates. For senior and business-critical hiring, you’ll coordinate complex interview processes and create a high-touch experience from the first interaction through to in-person interviews in our Dublin office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside candidate experience, you’ll help us continually improve how Recruiting operates across EMEA, using technology, data, AI and automation to make our processes simpler and more effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role requiring a minimum of two days per week in our Dublin office, with the flexibility to be on-site up to five days during busy periods or when candidate and business needs require it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with EMEA recruiters, understanding their priorities and helping keep hiring processes moving effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own interview coordination across EMEA, including complex scheduling across senior stakeholders, countries and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create thoughtful, memorable candidate experiences, ensuring candidates feel informed, welcomed and valued throughout the process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support senior and business-critical hiring, partnering with recruiters, senior leaders and Executive Assistants to deliver high-touch interview experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the in-person candidate experience in Dublin, working closely with Workplace and the wider People team to coordinate visits, welcome candidates and ensure interview days run seamlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships across our Dublin hub and act as an important connection point between Recruiting and the wider People organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work confidently across our recruiting technology ecosystem, including platforms such as Greenhouse, Workday and Tableau.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong data quality and support recruiting reporting and operational insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify, standardise and automate recruiting processes, including through AI and emerging technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global Recruiting Operations colleagues to implement programmes and continually improve how we work across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in recruiting coordination, recruiting operations, talent acquisition operations or a similarly fast-paced, people-focused environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organisation and the ability to independently manage complex logistics and competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong candidate and customer mindset, with an eye for the details that turn a good experience into a memorable one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence partnering with recruiters, senior leaders and Executive Assistants, with the judgement and discretion those relationships require.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with recruiting and People technology such as Greenhouse, Workday and Tableau, or strong technical aptitude and the ability to learn new systems quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with data and curious about how technology, AI and automation can improve recruiting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, solutions-focused approach and the ability to anticipate problems rather than simply react to them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and relationship-building skills across different teams, cultures and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
