&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK SMB Hunter team is responsible for winning net-new business across the SMB segment in the UK. We focus on bringing Stripe products to high-potential businesses that are not yet Stripe customers. We move with urgency, operate with focus, and pride ourselves on delivering strong commercial results through disciplined outbound execution and high-quality customer engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive on the UK SMB Hunter team, you will own a portfolio of prospective SMB accounts and be responsible for winning new business for Stripe. This is a true hunting role, with a strong emphasis on outbound prospecting, pipeline generation, and closing new logos. You will partner closely with an SDR to execute targeted outbound strategies, while also building your own pipeline through proactive prospecting and account-based selling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will run high-velocity, consultative sales cycles, help prospective users understand the value of the Stripe platform, and guide them from discovery through close and activation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle for net-new SMB prospects, from prospecting and discovery through solutioning, negotiation, close, and activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute outbound strategies across a named account set to create, progress, and close new business opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with SDRs to identify target accounts, refine messaging, and generate qualified pipeline, while also self-sourcing opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead consultative sales conversations with founders, operators, and functional stakeholders across payments, finance, product, and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand customer pain points and business objectives, and position Stripe products and solutions to meet their needs, while building trusted relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders throughout the sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal strategy and commercial negotiations to deliver strong outcomes for both Stripe and prospective users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high bar for pipeline quality, forecast accuracy, and operational rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in a closing sales role with a strong focus on net-new business acquisition, or in a customer-facing role such as solution engineering, implementation consulting, or strategy consulting with demonstrated experience influencing commercial outcomes and executive decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing outbound sales motions and building pipeline through a combination of SDR partnership and self-generated prospecting, or experience partnering closely with sales teams on account-based strategies that generate and progress new business opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to run high-velocity sales cycles while maintaining strong qualification, deal control, and forecasting discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consultative selling skills and the ability to uncover customer needs, build business cases, and align solutions to buyer priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical concepts and communicate the value of multi-product solutions to both business and technical stakeholders, with strong written and verbal communication skills in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling payments, fintech, SaaS, or other technology solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth sales environment with strong outbound expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with founders and SMB decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with account-based prospecting and territory planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the gross domestic product of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Benefits team is fundamental to the Stripe experience and directly supports our global workforce. The team ensures that our programs are competitive, clearly understood, and compliant with local regulations across 30 countries. We continually update our benefits strategy to meet the diverse needs of Stripe and Stripes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-role&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Benefits Program Manager plays a key role in shaping the strategy, execution, and user experience of our benefits programs. This role focuses primarily on benefits strategy and plan design, financial stewardship, vendor management, communications, the Stripe experience, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is suited to someone who can think strategically while supporting the successful execution of day-to-day operations and our broader benefits strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full lifecycle of our benefits programs, including market research, benchmarking, plan design, vendor selection and management, annual renewals and negotiations, communications, administration, security reviews, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor industry trends and regulatory changes, and recommend new or updated programs that align with Stripe’s business and Total Rewards strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert and develop clear communication plans that help Stripes understand our programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for benefits vendors, brokers, and third-party administrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and evaluate potential vendors, and manage the request for proposal process in partnership with Procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess vendor performance and manage contracts in partnership with Legal, ensuring that vendors meet their contractual commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compile, analyze, and report on key benefits metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with People Partners, People Consultants, Finance, Payroll, Employee Relations, and Legal to support a coordinated approach to our benefits strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance to manage the benefits budget, prepare cost projections, and evaluate the return on investment of new and existing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Workday and our benefits administration platform to improve workflows and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Systems to deliver key initiatives and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you’re encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 to 7 years of experience in a benefits role with similar responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and improving employee benefits programs using data, Stripe feedback, and financial analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of government regulations related to employee benefits and time off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing pension and time-off plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using benefits administration platforms, such as Workday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing stakeholders and negotiating contracts with benefits vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, growing environment, preferably in a technology company or large-scale organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to drive projects independently, identify and raise issues, and seek feedback when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment, with the ability to make decisions that align with Stripe’s culture and benefits strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing change initiatives related to benefits programs, including vendor or system implementations and transitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced data analysis and financial forecasting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mergers and acquisitions and benefits integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a high potential candidate to join Stripe’s Alliances and Channels (A&amp;amp;C) team as a Channel Sales Executive. The Channel Sales Executive (CSE) is a key part of the Alliances and Channels team, supporting platform partners that embed Stripe technology into their solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a dynamic Channel Sales professional to drive business growth with a portfolio of SaaS Platforms. You will identify high-value opportunities, develop demand with these platforms, and foster new business within our partner ecosystem. Working closely with Partner Development Managers and Stripe Account Executives, you will be responsible for delivering incremental growth of new users and revenue through your portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive joint go-to-market and co-selling initiatives with a designated and diverse portfolio of SaaS platforms in a channel sales motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with platform counterparts to drive net new demand for partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable Stripe and partner sales teams on the joint value proposition and lead account mapping workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute sales strategies to expand Stripe’s revenue with strategic platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the full deal cycle with partners, from sourcing new pipeline, opportunity progression to closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an advocate for partners within Stripe, representing Stripe within the partner&#39;s organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate sales and partner activities in Salesforce.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Who you are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technology sales experience with a proven track record of exceeding sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the payments, commerce, and/or Q2C landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales experience working in multi-party sales pursuits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to speak to functional leadership both internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead and be a team player on cross-functional deal pursuit teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel (25%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and execute territory and opportunity-specific plans leveraging tools such as Salesforce and Crossbeam.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Security Systems and Infrastructure (CSI) team safeguards Stripe’s people, offices, and operations by designing, delivering, and maintaining secure infrastructure across our global workplace portfolio. We take an intelligence-led, risk-based approach and partner closely with Workplace, IT, Security Operations, Legal, and external vendors to build reliable, scalable physical security systems and transition them to our Global Security Operations Center (GSOC) for ongoing monitoring and support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Corporate Security Infrastructure Project Manager, you will lead the security infrastructure workstream for new offices, expansions, relocations, and major workplace upgrades, with an initial focus on Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA) and support for global projects as needed. You will manage projects from early site assessment and design through installation, testing, commissioning, and operational handover.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be accountable for scope, schedule, budget, risk, quality, and stakeholder alignment across a portfolio of concurrent projects. In addition to delivering individual projects, you will strengthen the CSI program by improving standards, documentation, vendor performance, reporting, and repeatable project management processes. You will work through ambiguity, surface decisions early, and communicate clearly with technical teams, business partners, vendors, and senior leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end delivery of security infrastructure for office construction and expansion projects, from site assessment and requirements definition through design, procurement, installation, testing, commissioning, and closeout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead requests for proposals (RFPs) for security installations, including defining scope and requirements, coordinating bidders, reviewing submissions, evaluating proposals with relevant stakeholders, and supporting vendor selection recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project scope, schedule, budget, risks, dependencies, decisions, and change control; provide clear, outcome-focused reporting to stakeholders and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate security designs and technical requirements with Workplace, IT, Security Operations, Legal, architects, general contractors, landlords, and other project partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review design drawings, specifications, bills of materials, and implementation plans to ensure alignment with CSI standards and local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage security integrators, consultants, and contractors, including statements of work, delivery milestones, quality expectations, service levels, and performance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee system installation, acceptance testing, commissioning, punch-list resolution, documentation, and first-day-of-business readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure completed projects are smoothly handed over to the GSOC and support teams, with accurate system records, operating procedures, training, and ownership established.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve global construction standards, technical specifications, project templates, runbooks, and closeout documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and track project health metrics, vendor KPIs, budget forecasts, and lessons learned; use insights to improve delivery quality, predictability, and cost efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new market and site evaluations by identifying security risks, infrastructure constraints, integration needs, and mitigation options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the security repair and maintenance program, with a focus on the EMEA region, collaborating with regional teams to triage, track, and resolve security system and hardware issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CSI engineers and program leadership to prioritize work, resolve cross-project dependencies, and scale consistent processes across the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 25%, including international travel, to support site assessments, project milestones, commissioning, and handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of project management experience delivering complex physical security, workplace technology, low-voltage, construction, or similarly technical infrastructure projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing multiple concurrent projects across the full lifecycle, with ownership of scope, schedule, budget, risk, quality, and stakeholder communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating cross-functional delivery among technical teams, business partners, design and construction teams, vendors, and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong vendor and contractor management skills, including defining requirements, managing contracts or statements of work, tracking delivery, and addressing performance issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to translate technical details into clear decisions, risks, tradeoffs, and next steps for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment and structured problem-solving skills; able to operate independently, navigate ambiguity, anticipate issues, and drive timely decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous attention to detail and a demonstrated commitment to accurate documentation, standards, and operational handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing project management processes, tracking performance metrics, and applying lessons learned to improve future delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of physical security systems such as access control, video management, intrusion detection, intercoms, low-voltage infrastructure, and door hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel internationally up to 25%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering security infrastructure for offices in multiple countries or regions, particularly in EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Genetec Security Center, including Synergis, Omnicast, Security Center SaaS, or Stratocast; active Genetec certification is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with system integrations, networking fundamentals, APIs, webhooks, or cloud-managed security technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing budgets, forecasts, vendor KPIs, SLAs, and portfolio-level reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using project management and workflow tools such as Jira and Smartsheet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing and marking up construction and security design documentation using Bluebeam Revu or a similar PDF design-review tool, along with knowledge of commissioning practices and relevant local codes or regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in project management, construction management, security management, information technology, engineering, or a related field; or a relevant professional certification such as PMP, PRINCE2, ASIS PSP/CPP, or SIA CSPM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to select and use appropriate AI tools to improve work, while critically evaluating and refining outputs for accuracy and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Business Services’ (GBS) primary goal is to ensure operational excellence across deal cycles, increase revenue through the development of transformative commercial constructs, and drive closure of Stripe’s sold portfolio. The team&#39;s reach is widespread across Stripe, not exclusive to one sales segment or geographical region. GBS drives change across go-to-market, positively impacting Stripe users and cross-functional teams. GBS priorities are set through the direction of Stripe leadership and executive vision, partnership with sales and cross-functional organizations, as well as user feedback and market insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Business Services (GBS) team is looking for a Deal Strategist to focus on the closure of custom and standard commercial deals. You&#39;ll be responsible for deal lifecycle management and supporting cross-organizational alignment. This role requires a background in driving custom commercial and pricing deals to closure, a strong understanding of private pricing frameworks, as well as experience supporting sales through negotiations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have experience with subscription products, pricing strategies, and a background in supporting selling motions. You have strong communication skills. You&#39;ll love this job if you are a natural relationship and mechanism builder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work directly with sales teams, sales leaders, services and support teams, and customers to advise on deal structures, establish compelling commercials, and drive closure of customer issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the business and technical requirements of our customers and partners, advising sales teams on the best approach (balancing risk between custom terms and internal system limitations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove internal blockers between cross-functional teams such as Product, Legal, Finance, Accounting, Service Teams, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the sales cycle to ensure the deal terms align with Stripe goals, strategic vision is met, and closes as forecasted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial and legal agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the pricing and structuring of multithreaded product use cases in all segments and industries, especially in highly competitive sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly build credibility and trust with internal customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a clear and concise communicator, able to simplify complex concepts, influence stakeholders, and advocate for our Deal team as a strategic partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics with&amp;nbsp;4+ years of experience in deal management, procurement, pricing strategy, or financial consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in ambiguous, quickly scaling environments, comfortable with high-agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, presentation, negotiation, and project management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Payments and SaaS, and redlining agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Salesforce and Ironclad&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;AI fluency and passion for applying emerging technology efficiencies in the day-to-day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience training or enabling sales teams on pricing, quoting, and contract best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Education Partnerships team creates meaningful learning and engagement opportunities for students. We collaborate with educational institutions and community partners to design experiences that welcome students and help them explore future possibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team plans and delivers education initiatives and events of varying sizes, including the Stripe Young Scientist and Technology Exhibition (YSTE), University of Limerick’s Immersive Software Engineering (UL ISE), Patch and Irish Mathematical Trust (IMT).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Education Partnerships Coordinator, you’ll help bring Stripe’s education events and initiatives to life. You’ll work closely with the program lead and internal and external partners to design student experiences, coordinate events, and ensure that participants feel welcomed and supported.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers the opportunity to build expertise in education programming and event delivery while gradually taking on more complex projects and responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and project manage meaningful experiences for the student community through events and other engagement activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the programs lead to design the student experience and deliver large-scale events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Welcome students, provide clear guidance, and help ensure that their experiences run smoothly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate event logistics, schedules, materials, communications, and other operational details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Stripe’s existing education events and partnerships, including YSTE, UL ISE, Patch and IMT events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a thorough understanding of Stripe’s education initiatives and take ownership of increasingly complex responsibilities over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating events, programs, community activities, or comparable projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple workstreams, deadlines, and logistical details in a changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and thoughtful written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A welcoming and service-oriented approach to working with students, partners, and colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with internal teams and external organisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting education, student, early-career, or community programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating large-scale or multi-partner events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in learning about education partnerships and developing broader program-management responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deal Pricing is a dedicated global function that provides deal pricing expertise, financial insights, and deal support for negotiated users to Stripe&#39;s global Go-to-Market teams. We work to ensure deals create economic value for Stripe by establishing the deal commercial framework for a scaling sales organization, actively supporting large or complex deals, and providing pricing insights and feedback to sales, finance, and product leaders. Deal Pricing frequently works with cross-functional business partners across Operations, Finance and Strategy, and Product and there&#39;s constant collaboration with Deal Pricing colleagues across all regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be instrumental in providing thought leadership to regional sales teams and senior executives and continuing to develop our framework, approach, and associated processes in order to achieve mutually beneficial deals with our sold users while mitigating risk to Stripe. In addition to providing key financial insights and recommendations to business partners and Stripe leadership, you&#39;ll have a chance to stretch beyond the boundaries of finance through business case development and commercial negotiations with all types of customers across the full suite of Stripe&#39;s financial and payment products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key financial and strategic thought partner to specific EMEA Go-to-Market sales teams and their leadership in both pricing deals at scale and pricing strategic deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage pricing approvals and escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement our pricing and margin guidance and identify levers for commercial uplift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help refine frameworks and processes to evaluate deals and manage pricing activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain up-to-date pricing benchmarks and contribute to team analytical design and production efforts, using this data to enhance our pricing philosophy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in finance or deal pricing at a company, or experience within investment banking or management consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build collaborative working relationships with business partners through a combination of influencing and awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment by driving business results without significant supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent financial modeling, verbal, and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using LLMs and AI agents to conduct research, analyses, and automate work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the payments or technology sector&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CPQ solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting findings and recommendations to senior leadership, preferably to sales or go-to-market business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Developer Productivity group is responsible for making Stripe’s developers happy and productive. We work on tools, processes, and code refactoring to accelerate Stripe engineering as Stripe scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people with an interest in building the tools to improve the day to day experience of Engineers in Stripe. The ideal candidate will have a mix of technical expertise in either language processing tools, version control systems, contract testing, build systems, but most importantly a passion for solving developer experience problems, and a pragmatic ability to ship results iteratively. You’ll be working on a mix of fault tolerant distributed systems and also software which runs on individual developer machines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work with a code base of several million lines of code (and counting), used by hundreds of engineers across the globe, who initiate dozens of build jobs per minute. What we do is key to allowing Stripe engineers working in our main business logic layer to have the most productive time of their careers while building and running the features that Stripe and its customers need in order to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Efficiently scaling a fleet of 10,000s of CI workers, balancing the competing priorities of minimising user-facing queuing while also minimising cost and increasing reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering-wide initiatives as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the end-to-end experience of how our users engage with CI. This includes working with our users to understand pain points, and deliver incremental, or step-change improvements to their day-to-day workflows across multiple languages, with a higher focus on Java and Ruby.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing &amp;amp; maintaining state-of-the-art developer tooling and increasing tooling reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with other Stripe leaders to design and lead developer productivity best practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower the engineering team to achieve a high level of technical productivity, reliability, and simplicity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit great engineers, in collaboration with Stripe’s recruiting team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help engineers advance in their careers and develop new skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with your users to ensure the capabilities they need to safely, and reliably, deploy to production are available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting efficient inter-service testing to support teams developing new services, or migrating existing services, to Stripe’s modern service oriented architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building tools that are used daily by other developers (e.g. CI, build support, devboxes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for supporting developer productivity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully recruited and built great teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive writing and in-person communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have managed teams that designed and operated critical infrastructure, particularly with a broad remit across core capabilities, builds, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are empathetic to customer needs but visionary enough to not just deliver a faster horse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable planning in quarters, and can set a vision for several years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are excited about collaborating with teammates across Stripe’s organization, to provide a wonderful user experience for key developer workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our growing, global Product Support team, you&#39;ll be a critical driver in delivering excellent user experiences. This role goes beyond basic troubleshooting—it&#39;s about using your technical expertise, problem-solving mindset, and project management skills to strategically improve our support systems, processes, and product quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own complex technical user issues and coordinate with cross-functional teams, including Engineering and Product, to drive them to resolution. A deep understanding of SQL and APIs allows you to engage with these teams effectively, analyse data to inform decisions, and propose solutions that drive operational efficiency. Your work focuses on scaling support operations, creating better user experiences, and pushing forward continuous improvements that align with our key metrics, such as Consumer Satisfaction (CSAT), Contact Rate, and Service Level Agreements (SLA).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse and troubleshoot complex technical issues through direct user interaction (email, phone), utilising SQL to extract and interpret data, and leveraging your knowledge of API documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop product and platform expertise, working closely with Engineering, Product, and Operations teams to diagnose and resolve user issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategically optimise and scale support processes to enhance efficiency and improve the overall user experience, incorporating data-driven insights and metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead continuous improvement initiatives aimed at hitting key performance metrics such as Consumer Satisfaction (CSAT), Contact Rate, and SLA compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and refine documentation to empower users to resolve issues via self-service, reducing dependency on support teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with and advocate to Product and Engineering to proactively improve the platform based on user feedback, ensuring long-term product reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional projects aimed at identifying inefficiencies in current processes and driving the implementation of long-term solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Constantly challenge the status quo and push for innovation in user support strategies and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a customer-facing product support role, with a focus on troubleshooting technical issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL for data analysis and querying, with the ability to interpret datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills, capable of diagnosing complex issues and driving them to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in stakeholder management, with the ability to influence cross-functional teams and drive progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in project management, particularly in optimising processes, workflows, or support operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work occasional weekends and holidays (with compensatory time off).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data analysis skills and a passion for interpreting data to improve decision-making and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable explaining technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in technical environments and the ability to diagnose and resolve highly technical user issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Collaboration team helps Stripe employees work smarter and more efficiently, get to know each other, and request and receive help from one another. The team is nimble and creative. We work across a wide stack; on any given day, we discuss user interface design, data models, API design, infrastructure maintenance, agentic integrations, or all of the above. We’re excited to innovate in a space that traditionally isn’t thought of as in the forefront of innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being a small team, we carefully choose what we work on to have the highest leverage. This is not always easy—we work very cross-functionally, partnering with groups from engineering to Communications to senior leadership. But one of our greatest rewards is getting to sit next to and see the impact our work has on our users: our fellow Stripe employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an engineer on Stripe’s Collaboration team, you will be a key member of a team that acts as a force multiplier on the internal tools that Stripe uses. You will focus on building innovative AI-native experiences that help Stripe employees be more productive across various tasks and activities. You’ll collaborate with other teams across Stripe, combine traditional hands-on engineering with emerging AI capabilities, and experiment with different ideas and approaches to empower and delight your users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a team of smart, motivated engineers who put their users first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own solutions from end to end, managing complexity and engaging directly with stakeholders to think through everything from success metrics to MCP tooling to the nitty-gritty implementation details of the products you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage the latest AI tooling to refine and optimize both your users’ workflows and your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use both qualitative and quantitative metrics to determine priorities and measure effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold Stripe’s high standards for engineering and product quality and mentor newer team members to do the same.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 6+ years of professional software engineering experience, including 2+ years of industry experience building rich web experiences using modern frameworks such as React, Vue, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well across a full stack, from user experience to workflow automations to reliability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working directly with users and cross-functional partners to build creative solutions that address their problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to think rigorously, navigate ambiguity, and make hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working together with your team toward common goals, but are also able to drive your work forward autonomously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a passion for enabling people to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an interest in partnering with creative, non-technical teams, such as those responsible for Stripe’s creative communications and publishing efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of shipping LLM-powered experiences with a strong understanding of how underlying technologies work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have industry experience working with Ruby, TypeScript, and React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are experienced with using AI tools to maximize your technical throughput while maintaining a high bar for quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You never lose sight of the end user, and you enjoy the quick feedback loops made possible by working (sometimes literally) next to your users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building the economic engine for AI – and it’s working. Today, 88% of the Forbes AI 50 are building on Stripe (and most of the remaining 12% are pre-monetization).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI GTM team is focused on helping AI-native businesses monetize and scale. We&#39;re in a unique position—partnering with the world&#39;s most ambitious AI companies (like OpenAI, Anthropic, ElevenLabs, and NVIDIA) to help them grow. This is one of the fastest growing parts of the business, and we need more great people to help us continue to accelerate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sales Manager on the EMEA Startup team at Stripe, you will leverage your sales leadership and product expertise to drive growth through existing strategic AI customers. Reporting to the Regional Sales Lead for Startups, you will lead a team of Account Executives responsible for expanding Stripe&#39;s relationship with some of the most important European AI companies in the world—across payments, billing, and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be instrumental in leading in-depth product discussions with customers, developing consultative and solution-based sales strategies, and building deep knowledge of the AI industry and its unique monetization challenges. You will collaborate closely with Product, Marketing, Product Marketing, and User Operations teams to develop and execute against our go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the long-term vision for a growing AI GTM team and scale day-to-day operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a team of Account Executives managing existing AI accounts (driving revenue expansion, product attach, and retention) and looking for new business opportunities. Establish strategic plans and objectives to drive growth across the AI GTM business line, guiding execution to KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop a high-performing team, fostering a strong culture of energized and engaged Stripes while investing in the growth and development of your team. Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based sales skills throughout the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for driving revenue, increasing product attach rates, and growing existing clients at high rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product, Marketing, and User Operations teams to influence our product roadmap (you are on the frontier!) and accelerate our growth trajectory for our AI industry users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as both an internal and customer-facing expert on Stripe&#39;s products, particularly as they apply to AI-native business models (usage-based billing, marketplace payments, embedded finance, agentic commerce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with customer executives (CEO, CFO, CTO) and serve as a trusted advisor on how Stripe can support their growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create best practices and improve the business and customer engagement model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales leader: &lt;/strong&gt;You are an adept sales leader, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization. You see value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require both deep product understanding and technical knowledge, especially for AI industry users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People developer: &lt;/strong&gt;You are a strong people leader who builds high-performing teams through coaching, accountability, and culture. You&#39;re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives) and are excited to become an expert and share your knowledge. You possess an organized, self-starter mindset and excellent communication skills, with a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI enthusiast:&lt;/strong&gt; You have deep context in the AI industry and are energized by keeping up with new developments in the space. You bring a user-first mindset— you approach every customer interaction as a consultative partner rather than a transactional seller.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technically curious:&lt;/strong&gt; You understand APIs, webhooks, and modern developer tools—and you can hold credible conversations with engineering leaders about how Stripe&#39;s infrastructure fits into their stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales leadership experience, launching and growing high-functioning sales teams/products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in hyper-growth SaaS or technology environments&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success managing existing/growth customer portfolios and driving revenue expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to be a self-starter, capable of driving business results without significant supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of AI industry dynamics, business models, and monetization strategies (usage-based pricing, API-first distribution, agentic commerce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product acumen—ability to learn and articulate complex product capabilities, understand how they work technically, and connect them to user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including strong presentation skills for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke agreements with commercial and enterprise businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in payments, financial infrastructure, developer tools, or AI/ML platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships within the AI ecosystem (AI labs, AI-native SaaS companies, developer platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling complex platform solutions involving multiple products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth-stage software company or a leading payments/fintech company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe&#39;s product suite and how AI companies leverage financial infrastructure to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Financial Crime and Risk Oversight (FinCRO) team at Stripe exists to help protect Stripe and its users from crime. Our people play an important role in combating financial crime across a global footprint and in enabling Stripe to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The global team works as a cohesive whole to manage and mitigate financial crime risks and meet and exceed the expectations of our users, our financial partners, and our regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are a deeply caring group of folks, slightly obsessed with our tradecraft, dedicated to protecting our users and the financial ecosystem from crime, and committed to our work, our lives, and our hobbies with equal passion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help us protect Stripe and its users from crime and grow our Financial Crime and Risk Oversight (FinCRO) team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced financial crime professional to lead our financial crimes program in Ireland (Stripe Technology Europe, Limited [STEL]). In this role, you will lead and be primarily responsible for managing financial crime risk at Stripe in Ireland and for our European operations. This will include branches of STEL in other European jurisdictions. You will be the principal decision-maker on financial crime risk management decisions, serving a critical role in ensuring Stripe’s continued safe growth and success in the region. You’ll also be heavily involved in the strategic design and planning of Stripe’s financial crimes program as we enhance and uplevel controls and operations. You will be the leading expert on financial crime matters, advising on the evolution of financial crime regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is both a technology company and a financial services company, and you will need to be comfortable straddling both of those worlds every day. The right person for the role will be enthusiastic both about the mission of anti-financial crime and about the application of new and innovative technology approaches to protect Stripe, its users, the financial system, and the community at large from crime. The role holder will also enjoy seeking creative solutions and moving quickly, often in the face of ambiguity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additionally, in your role as the STEL Money Laundering Reporting Officer (MLRO), based in Ireland, you will be the public face of Stripe’s financial crimes compliance team in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Stripe’s global compliance and financial crimes frameworks, policies, programs, and controls (e.g., KYC, transaction monitoring, regulatory reporting, sanctions, and risk assessment) incorporate local regulatory requirements and industry best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that all transactions identified as potentially suspicious are investigated and reviewed in accordance with established procedures, and that appropriate escalations are made and measures are taken to mitigate Stripe’s risk exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set, lead, and manage the culture of risk and compliance across the team in the local business, and work with our group and regional Legal, Risk, Financial Crime, and Compliance teams to define our risk appetite in the local market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee financial crimes compliance for Stripe’s operations in Ireland and the EU, including the regulated businesses in Ireland&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance to the business teams on existing and upcoming regulatory requirements and resulting potential product changes, and provide strategic advice on expansion initiatives in Ireland and the EU from a financial crimes perspective, both enabling Stripe’s growth and advising on risk mitigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a thought leader in supporting and driving innovative, technology-focused compliance solutions with regulators and financial partners, and build and maintain Stripe’s relationships with financial crimes counterparts at our partner financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the team’s other compliance officers to build a global program by contributing to strategic planning, goal setting, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years’ experience in an AML/CFT role and comfort juggling numerous aspects of an AML/CFT compliance program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience executing complex financial crimes initiatives and rolling out large-scale compliance initiatives (onboarding preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work efficiently and independently in a fast-paced, high-volume environment and cross-functionally with internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An effective and relatable “culture of compliance” mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PCF-52 experience in Ireland and equivalent experience in other European markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments or fintech experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Related regulatory experience, such as anti-bribery and corruption, payments, international policy, or audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAMS, CFE, or ICA certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional European languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Renewals Team partners with account teams to deliver successful contract renewals, protect margins, and grow Stripe’s existing revenue base. We bring commercial expertise to renewal planning and execution, including understanding historical consumption and pricing, positioning customer value, identifying risk, and surfacing upsell and cross-sell opportunities. Our focus is on building a proactive, consistent renewal motion that delivers strong outcomes for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the head of EMEA &amp;amp; APAC Renewals, you will lead a distributed team of Renewals Specialists and build regional refinement on a globally consistent model, including driving a proactive renewal motion across the two regions. You will partner with global and regional Sales leaders, Customer Success, Sales Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, and other internal partners to translate global priorities into regional plans, strengthen account-team engagement, and scale how we support renewals across markets and customer segments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercial leader who combines strong renewal and negotiation judgment with the ability to build high-performing teams and durable operating processes. You will bring clarity in an ambiguous, high-growth environment, turn commercial insights into action, and build trusted partnerships with field leaders at every level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the EMEA and APAC renewals strategy, translating global priorities into regional and segment-specific plans that improve retention, support expansion, and protect sustainable commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a proactive renewal motion with Sales and Customer Success, establishing early account planning, clear responsibilities, and consistent specialist partnerships. Enable engagement 12–18 months ahead of renewal where appropriate to the customer segment and deal complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted partnerships across account executives and front-line, second-line, and regional sales leaders, ensuring renewal insights inform account and territory plans and translate into clear action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a rigorous regional operating cadence for renewal forecasting, risk inspection, deal strategy, and escalation. Turn portfolio insights into actionable recommendations for field leaders and track follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design team coverage and capacity plans that balance strategic deal support with scalable engagement across the renewal portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Renewals Specialists, strengthening negotiation skills, commercial judgment, and strategic account-team partnership while supporting individual career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic guidance on complex renewals and serve as an executive sponsor or senior escalation partner for key customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale shared playbooks, systems, and AI-enabled workflows, with clear quality standards, human review, and accountability for adoption and delivery. Maintain a consistent global baseline while adapting execution to regional and segment needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface recurring customer and commercial insights to inform improvements to renewal playbooks, tooling, and cross-functional execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in renewals, customer success, account management, or technology sales, including 5+ years of people leadership, with a demonstrated track record of delivering retention and growth outcomes for existing customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading geographically distributed commercial teams across multiple markets and cultures, with the ability to adapt engagement models to regional and customer-segment needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading complex renewal or existing-customer negotiations, balancing customer value, retention, expansion, pricing, and sustainable commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build trusted partnerships with senior Sales and Customer Success leaders, align teams around shared priorities, and establish clear responsibilities in a matrixed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building proactive renewal engagement models that bring account teams together early to identify risks, establish account strategies, and uncover expansion opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and operational judgment, including renewal forecasting, performance inspection, and translating customer consumption, pricing, and commercial data into clear recommendations and action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and scaling team coverage, capacity plans, and repeatable operating processes in a high-growth technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, coach, and retain high-performing teams, strengthening both commercial judgment and strategic account-team partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate long-term strategy into clear priorities, delivery commitments, and measurable execution, while operating effectively through ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication skills, with the ability to advise senior stakeholders and engage directly in strategic customer negotiations and escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a dedicated renewals organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across both EMEA and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payments, financial infrastructure, or consumption-based commercial models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying automation and AI to improve commercial workflows, with clear standards for adoption, quality, and human review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Account Management, Support and Services (TAMSS) supports Stripe’s largest, fastest-growing, and most strategically important users through our paid support offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Account Managers serve as trusted advisers to users and account teams. They combine an understanding of a user’s business, Stripe integration, technical architecture, and strategic priorities to improve integration performance and resilience, lead complex engagements, and coordinate Stripe’s response to critical issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The EMEA organization supports direct merchants and platforms across a diverse set of markets, industries, and technical environments. The team partners closely with Sales, Customer Success, Product, Engineering, Support, Professional Services, and Solutions Architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Technical Account Management for Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA), you will own the regional direction and performance of TAMSS, including teams supporting Stripe’s largest direct merchants and platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll translate Stripe’s global priorities into regional plans that reflect EMEA’s markets, users, and commercial opportunities. Your remit will include user outcomes, service quality, paid support growth, organizational health, and the effective allocation of TAM capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also serve as an executive partner for strategically important users and represent EMEA on the global TAMSS leadership team. Insights from the region will inform how Stripe develops its products, services, and approach to supporting complex users around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the multi-year strategy and operating model for EMEA TAMSS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and scale a substantial, distributed EMEA Technical Account Management organization, developing a strong management layer across multiple markets, user segments, and technical domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional outcomes across paid support growth, service delivery, strategic-user health, technical impact, and organizational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine the regional organization and coverage model, including leadership structure, market coverage, capacity allocation, and investment priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders across Sales, Customer Success, Product, Engineering, Support, Professional Services, and Solutions Architecture to deliver coordinated outcomes for users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with go-to-market leaders on paid support adoption, renewals, account strategy, staffing, and the sustainable growth of Stripe’s services business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with executive technical and business leaders at Stripe’s largest users, serving as a senior escalation point when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide executive oversight for high-impact user escalations and critical support incidents, ensuring clear ownership, rapid coordination, timely communication, and effective resolution, translating learnings into support experience improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use user feedback, commercial insights, and operational data to identify risks, improve performance, and inform investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn patterns from complex user engagements into improvements to Stripe’s products, services, and operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and develop managers, set clear expectations, and build a strong succession pipeline for critical leadership roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent EMEA in global TAMSS planning and develop approaches that can be adopted across other regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in technical account management, solutions architecture, customer success, or related user-facing technical functions, including 6+ years managing people and experience managing managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading substantial, distributed organizations through multiple organizational layers, developing managers, and retaining strong management and technical talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting multi-year strategy and translating it into organizational plans, investment decisions, and measurable user and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building trusted relationships with executive business and technical leaders at large and strategically important users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical and commercial judgment, including the ability to understand complex integrations, assess user and service-delivery risks, and work effectively with Product and Engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success aligning senior leaders with different priorities around a shared strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with P&amp;amp;L management, budget ownership, or operating in a General Manager (GM) capacity for a regional services organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a technical services organization across multiple EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing and delivering paid technical services, support plans, or another recurring services offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial technology, payments, Software as a Service, or API-based products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting global enterprises or platforms with complex technical and operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Incident Ops team is a global 24/7 team responsible for driving incident response and management from detection to resolution. Stripe is proud of its five 9s reliability and this team is at the forefront of ensuring we keep it that way - working hand-in-hand with Reliability Eng and across the Tech Org. This team of incident response managers (IRM) is defined by our sense of ownership and how we drive incidents to resolution - marshaling the necessary cross-functional resources to respond to and resolve service outages, critical bugs, security attacks and anything that significantly impacts the users of our products. The team is user-first and ensures appropriate external communications from Stripe and senior management to keep our users informed of disruption to their experience of Stripe. The team is skilled in communications, incident handling and technical adeptness as incidents can arise from anywhere and cut across products and orgs in Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Incident Response Manager (IRM), you’ll play the key role in driving the right level of response from Stripes to incidents, determining impact, rallying Stripes to mitigate, communicating to users and ensuring appropriate remediations and orchestrate the Root Cause Analysis (RCA) process. You’ll work hand-in-hand with IRMs and engineers globally to ensure solid 24/7 coverage on how we monitor, detect, respond, communicate and mitigate incidents. When not managing incidents, you&#39;ll help scale our ability to respond to incidents, improve our operations, analyze data to provide insights and deepen our technical expertise in products. As a result, you’ll be seen as the protector of our users - in minimizing the impact of incidents on their business and ensuring that Stripe is always thinking of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an on-call Incident Commander, responsible for driving and managing incident resolution with a high level of urgency, cross-functional collaboration, and accuracy, while partnering with a global and diverse set of teams, including Engineering, Product, Policy, Risks, PR, Legal, Execs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead all user-facing incidents across domains at Stripe - including reliability, technical, security, and data privacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&quot;User First&quot; approach to determine impact, providing accurate situation reports, facilitating comms bridges, and ensuring useful and timely external communications to users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively update internal stakeholders, make decisions through data and influence by partnering with Engineering, Sales, Support and other cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the root cause analysis process while conducting post-mortems, remediations identification, and ensure problem management tasks meet SLA and user expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive improvements in the incident handling process and incident management metrics and tooling based on trends and data of Stripe&#39;s incidents in collaboration with engineering, product and operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to processes, projects, forums, or groups that impact and grow team culture positively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of demonstrable major incident experience for organizations that run mission critical applications or always-on Saas environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead multiple incidents concurrently with authority and influence responders with agency and reasoning skills to resolve ambiguous problems and drive to root cause.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate understanding of application development, application architectures, and applications deployed in cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of infrastructure, including physical, virtual, and container-based compute platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated quantitative, and analytical skills in data manipulation using SQL, Splunk or other tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent task management skills, must be detail-oriented with ability to remain composed, methodical, and think fast in a high-pressured environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal English communication skills, with the ability to translate complex technical issues for internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain expertise in classes of incidents such as technical, privacy, security or crisis with a strong desire to continuously learn about Stripe&#39;s products, technical issues and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to review complex technical details regarding ongoing issues/events and convey the key details to senior stakeholders to facilitate real-time decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with broad user-facing communications (e.g. status pages, tweets) and/or targeted communications (e.g. direct emails, support ticket responses).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity operating or managing distributed architectures with the ability to correlate system behaviors based on known inter-dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated understanding of full stack development and support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Professional Services team works with our most strategic users. You will work on the highest visibility projects to provide technical expertise to our customers to help accelerate their knowledge, solution design and integrations with Stripe. This role is responsible for leading strategic conversations and developing plans that will transform the payments and financial infrastructure for leading enterprises. We&#39;re building an AI-first team. Using AI to work efficiently, and to deliver faster and better outcomes for our users, will be a key part of this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute integration engineering end-to-end, from high-level architecture down to code implementation. This includes conducting discovery sessions with users to understand their goals, parsing out specific use cases, and guiding users to implement high complexity integrations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think on your feet and communicate technical concepts, explaining how Stripe works from both a product feature and API architecture perspective. Manage user expectations on timelines and product changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the primary, ongoing technical point of contact for our largest users&#39; and partners&#39; technical teams. You will be responsible for resolving user integration issues and owning escalations for operational issues and priority requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI across the engagement lifecycle to reduce manual effort, accelerate delivery, and improve the quality of what we hand to users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Sales, Solution Architecture and Implementation teams to drive client engagement, customer wins, and revenue on behalf of the Professional Services team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product and Engineering to proactively identify potential enhancements and new features based on feedback you’ll gather from the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep technical support and debugging, inspecting and understanding the Stripe codebase and thoroughly testing functionality to best advise users, while also building and demonstrating proof-of-concept integrations, creating user-specific test plans, and answering ad-hoc technical questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In some cases, lead &quot;Hands On Keyboard&quot; implementations for user engagements, providing material feedback on coding practices, CI/CD, and software architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and optimize existing user integrations and provide recommendations to improve performance, reliability, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tools and analytics; create dashboards, run queries, and generate custom data reports to support user business reviews and operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and share knowledge, building reusable processes to enable the larger Professional Services team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years + experience in a Software Engineering / Integration Engineering role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write code (in programming languages like Go, Java, C/C++ etc.) and quickly debug user code snippets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with various code-level debugging (Stripe code and user code) and using code as a tool for problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong generalist technical experience, including proficiency in SQL and an understanding of data structures and algorithms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the payments domain and API security topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be comfortable talking about technical concepts, and explaining how Stripe works, both from a product features and API architecture perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user first approach &amp;amp; empathy with our users, capable of mapping business requirements into reliable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident and comfortable with customers, with the ability to lead strategic technical conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI tools (e.g. coding assistants, LLM-based agents) to improve how you work, and a strong appetite to continue to build that experience quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy the puzzle of solving open-ended problems, both individually and as a member of our team.&lt;br&gt;Willingness to learn and teach others, including mentoring newer team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, communicative, consultative; able to apply specific methodologies to ensure repeatability of engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectually curious, with great problem solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical writing skills to document complex integration guidance and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To advance Stripe’s important mission, we are building a world class Internal Audit (IA) team. Our purpose is to strengthen the organization’s ability to create, protect, and sustain value by providing the board and management with independent, risk-based, and objective assurance, advice, insight, and foresight. We are consumed with the goal of moving as fast as the business, being powered by technology, and increasing the maturity of Stripe’s controls where it matters the most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our IA team is responsible for providing objective assurance on the design and operational effectiveness of Stripe’s internal controls and business processes, its compliance with laws and regulations, its risk management framework, and other governance processes. Organized as a single global function, the team operates under a unified methodology, set of policies, and governance model — with specialized leads who bring deep domain expertise while working in alignment with that shared framework. We’re looking for a leader with extensive finance, operations, fiduciary, and regulatory compliance audit experience who will help us build and scale a global audit program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior member of the EMEA IA team you will be central to shaping our audit landscape in one of the most dynamic sectors of FinTech. In this pivotal role, you will help drive the execution of a comprehensive, risk-based internal audit strategy that not only anticipates emerging risks but also aligns seamlessly with our management&#39;s vision and regulatory landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Internal Audit team, you will harness your expertise in governance, risk management, and internal controls to produce invaluable assessments that empower our Board, Audit Committee, and senior leadership to make informed, strategic decisions. This is more than just an auditing position; it&#39;s an opportunity to influence the very framework of our operations, protect our organization from unforeseen challenges, and bolster our commitment to excellence and compliance in the rapidly evolving world of Fintech. If you&#39;re looking to make a significant impact and elevate your career in an innovative and supportive environment, this is your chance to step into a role where your insights will drive meaningful change and ensure our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is office-based in Dublin, Ireland.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and execute risk-based internal audits and provide input into a risk-based internal audit strategy that ensures comprehensive, end-to-end audit coverage. This strategy should reflect emerging risks, management priorities, and regulatory obligations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee evaluation and testing of governance, risk management, internal controls, compliance, financial reporting, and operational processes to ensure their effectiveness, accuracy, and regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present independent, objective reports directly to senior leadership on the effectiveness of internal controls, risk management, and governance processes, communicating complex technical and regulatory risks to senior stakeholders in clear, actionable terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage with partners and regulators; help prepare and present audit evidence and findings to enhance confidence in our internal oversight processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly communicate complex risks and impacts to senior stakeholders, including the Board, Audit Committee, and regulators (e.g., FCA, CBI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior management and cross-functional teams - including engineering, product, treasury, legal, compliance, and operations - to translate audit findings into durable, structured remediation plans with control enhancements, tracking all corrective actions to verified closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invest in understanding the business to better identify areas of need and opportunities to advise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and stay current on applicable regulatory requirements and (e.g., GAAP, IFRS, PSD2, EMD2, EBA, etc.), emerging trends and best practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in internal auditing, risk management, or compliance, preferably within the banking or financial services sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in auditing financial controls, operations and regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in risk-based audit planning, execution, and reporting across governance, compliance, financial reporting, and operational controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certification such as CIA, CPA, CAMS, CRCM or similar is required (or active pursuit).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with experience using data analytics and continuous monitoring tools to support audit activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills; ability to present complex issues clearly to non-technical senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead cross-functional remediation efforts and track closure of corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of integrity, independence, and professional skepticism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in Accounting, Finance, MBA, or related advanced degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a regulated financial institution or network with complex relationships among network partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with audit management software, automation platforms, and advanced data analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of building continuous audit/monitoring programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Employee Relations and People Risk &amp;amp; Compliance team is a relatively new center of excellence here at Stripe. We are striving to build a respectful, balanced, well-skilled team focused on enabling the People team, managers, and ICs to navigate challenging career moments while balancing compliance, empathy, and risk, resulting in success and engagement for all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an exceptional leader for the Employee Relations, People Risk &amp;amp; Compliance function to join our team at Stripe with coverage for our locations in EMEA and APAC. This individual will have deep subject knowledge and expertise in employee relations, a strong understanding of people related risk in the regulatory space and will be an instrumental player/coach, who will lead the team focusing on improving and implementing frameworks, guidelines, approaches, and best practices. The International Employee Relations, People Risk &amp;amp; Compliance Leader&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;will be highly cross functional and collaborative, partnering to inform and support Stripes and cross functional colleagues, both within and outside of the People team. This role reports into the Global Employee Relations, People Risk &amp;amp; Compliance leader at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Case Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support to or personally lead medium to high complexity employee relations investigations, making recommendations on appropriate courses of action, matching investigation strategy to the complexity, risk, sensitivity, and confidentiality of the investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance on complex performance management cases, depending on what support needs are determined with People Partners and People Consultants.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure cases are handled fairly, consistently, transparently, in a timely fashion, and in line with company culture, policies, and appropriate local laws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advising&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counsel People Partners, People Consultants, and business leaders on ER issues, trends and risks to foster sound business decisions, rooted in commerciality and aligned with Stripe’s Operating Principles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that optimal decisions are made by leaders, People Partners and other stakeholders through influencing, coaching, and by providing technical expertise and sound strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and refresh training offerings depending on company needs and external regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish best practices and frameworks for critical business and regulatory activities and/or policies, in partnership with our employment legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage proactive and positive relationships with works councils and unions where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the International team, building an exceptional performance bench&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect, analyze, interpret and make recommendations on ER related data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure alignment to the larger strategy of the People team and Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve, socialize and rollout processes, approaches, guidelines, practices and operating procedures to use in EMEA, APAC and globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement appropriate risk frameworks relevant to the People team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and conduct training for leaders, managers, employees, People Partners, People Consultants, Talent Partners, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain an organized case management system; ability to run analytics and metrics, produce dashboards, and drive monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree required; JD, MBA, or other Advanced Degree preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of Employee Relations/Human Resources experience managing complex global investigations and people related risk required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of direct management/supervisory experience leading cross-border teams required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting up and managing productive relationships with works councils and/or unions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive understanding of the regulatory environment in which Stripe operates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior written oral communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to remain positive, collaborative and objective while under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of positively influencing leaders, teams, and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be a coach, mentor, advise, and partner with stakeholders at varying levels of seniority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of ER, people risk labour relations, training, and conflict resolution, along with direct experience leading complex global investigations at all levels, including executive level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with and extensive experience in employment laws in the EMEA region (and APAC preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work under pressure and deal with complex issues, while maintaining composure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced decision maker who uses good reasoning and sound judgment required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be discreet and maintain confidentiality is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be self-motivated and have an enhanced ability to prioritize/plan in a fast-paced, high growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open to travel (some travel may be required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Partnerships team sits within the Global Partnerships organization and is a key component of our success. Our team is responsible for developing and managing relationships with the global and regional banks that enable the Stripe product strategy and deliver new capabilities to Stripe users. Our team executes on high-impact, cross-functional product partnership initiatives across existing products and early-stage &quot;up the stack&quot; financial products. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and are essential for us to offer products used by millions of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: This is not a commercial sales position - for those opportunities, see our Business Development roles&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Partner Development Manager to help manage out portfolio of international banks. You&#39;ll be responsible for developing and executing the multi-year, global strategies for building our relationships across many of our most important banking partners. You&#39;ll focus on designing, scaling, and continuously improving mechanisms to deepen relationships with our partners, as well as highly impactful programs key to differentiating Stripe. As part of these efforts, you&#39;ll collaborate closely with cross-functional stakeholders (including Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, Risk, etc.), and with the banking partners&#39; executive teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will have a demonstrated ability to manage and develop partners, think strategically and apply diagnostic thinking to business, product, and technical challenges, and earn trust with and influence others. A high-agency attitude, the ability to raise expectations in changing environments, and a drive to create impact through ownership are all important in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the go-to-partner strategy and execute on our most ambitious company-bending, bank-network-driven projects that are global and cross-border in nature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the banking partner plans, the overall economics, day-to-day operational excellence, and be responsible for driving the partnerships to successful outcomes for Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage banking, treasury, and payments industry knowledge to craft thoughtful partnership and product strategies with transaction banks, lenders, capital markets, central banks, and schemes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate, in partnership with Product, to execute deals supporting that strategy and help ensure a proper execution plan is in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage significant industry experience to educate and help internal teams compose our holistic bank-led strategy and to advance that strategy with banking partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9+ years of relevant experience in banking or fintech, including direct ownership of banking partnerships supporting collections, payouts, stored value, or embedded financial products. This is a specialised banking-infrastructure partnerships role, rather than a general fintech business-development role. The strongest candidates will combine commercial bank-partner ownership with evidence that they have taken a payments capability into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of the banking and clearing landscape across multiple geographies with specific focus on transaction banking, e-money, safeguarding, multi-currency, and cross-border payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building proprietary global collection and payout networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of working in a product-centric environment with significant internal and external dependencies across product, engineering, legal, sales, risk, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad and deep experience executing industry-wide partnership strategies to build innovative product experiences and go-to-market models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mission of Fraud Operations is to act as guardians of the global financial ecosystem by proactively reducing fraud, making it difficult and unprofitable for fraudsters to carry out attacks through Stripe. Fraud Ops is responsible for developing and maintaining scalable processes related to fraud analysis, card testing, account takeover, and financial partner investigation requests. We strive to improve manual fraud decisioning and enhance support experiences for users impacted by fraud decisions, all while enabling healthy growth for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Payments Fraud Investigator, you will play a critical role in safeguarding our financial ecosystem by investigating high-risk accounts and identifying various forms of fraud. You will conduct deep-dive analyses of merchant accounts, lead cross-functional projects, and collaborate with stakeholders to enhance our fraud detection and prevention strategies at scale. Your expertise in fraud patterns and typologies will be essential in developing and enhancing investigative processes and programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Analyze high-risk accounts to identify fraudulent merchants, card testing, account takeovers, and other fraud vectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Lead root cause analyses to identify gaps in current systems, policies, and strategies, and determine enhancements and process improvements to address emerging fraud risks through collaboration with key stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive cross-functional projects aimed at refining operational processes and tools, enhancing the detection and management of fraudulent accounts across our global analyst network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Investigate, mitigate, and remediate urgent fraud incidents, such as card testing and account takeover, and manage user responses to high-urgency distributed fraud attacks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Communicate regular updates during team and organization-wide business reviews, summarize outcomes of complex investigations for executives, and deliver clear case determinations to users and partner financial institutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Travel to vendor locations to conduct analyst training sessions and knowledge-sharing initiatives, while identifying challenges and enhancing analyst performance to improve overall outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• This role may require weekend coverage as part of an on-call rotation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 3+ years of experience conducting complex investigations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 1+ years of experience leading risk-related projects and initiatives, collaborating effectively with cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Demonstrated ability to leverage data to propose solutions for both tactical and strategic challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Proactive approach to challenging the status quo, with a willingness to question existing processes and advocate for improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• User-centric perspective when addressing challenges, balanced with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Ability to travel to vendor locations for up to 10% of the year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience in payments, e-commerce, social media, or fintech, mitigating digital or card-not-present fraud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience investigating and mitigating card testing and account takeover attacks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience designing fraud and risk workflows, analyst tooling, and process and procedural workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong proficiency using SQL to analyze data, drive insights, and create dashboards and visualizations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payments Performance Team identifies payment optimisation opportunities for Stripe’s merchants. The Global Payments Performance team serves a critical role both in demonstrating thought leadership on challenging payment topics, and also partnering with our high-potential merchants to set them up for long term success. We want a partnership with Stripe to be a competitive advantage for our customers, large and small, by providing them with best-in-class technology in concert with insightful and specific advice on how to harness this technology to achieve their business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Payments Performance EMEA team will be responsible for leading data-driven discussions with existing and prospective merchants on optimisation strategies across a variety of areas including, card network costs, acceptance, fraud, and cross-border flows to start. You will be instrumental in building our optimisation narratives/tools and delivering on our merchant engagement model. You will also collaborate with Sales, deploying your knowledge to differentiate Stripe to win deals, and partner with our Customer Success organization to ensure that merchants are successful working with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discussions with existing and prospective merchants, and provide the Sales team with tools and training to lead discussions with merchants and prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as both an internal and merchant-facing expert on payment optimisation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and build on Stripe’s wide-ranging payments expertise to create optimisation narratives/tools supported by rigorous analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use existing tools to deploy sophisticated optimisation playbooks and analyses across Stripe’s customer portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesise and relay customer feedback and our findings to inform Stripe’s product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide feedback on our tools and playbooks to help continuously improve our self serve offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in payments or operations at a leading technology company, or consultancy in the payments industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of e-commerce payments, cards based payments processing and optimisation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build collaborative working relationships with cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to be a self-starter capable of driving business results without significant supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting directly to merchants and serving as a subject matter expert providing both internal and customer-facing advisory in the payments domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop optimization playbooks and stay updated on industry best practices and Stripe innovations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering measurable improvements in payment acceptance, conversion, fraud outcomes or payment costs across a portfolio of underlying merchants or sellers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data processing, organizational and analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language proficiency in French is essential for this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, dashboard building, modeling, or reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of card network rules and regulations, local payment methods, and the regulatory environment (PSD2/PSD3)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting to senior business leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with SaaS Platform or marketplace business models is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe Connect or comparable platform-payments solutions, including connected-account models, payment flows, and the allocation of fees and risk responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the key drivers to our success is a committed and rigorous emphasis on our people. We believe that our competitive advantage lies in our talent and that we can build a sustainable advantage by attracting, enabling and cultivating the world’s most exceptional people to do the very best work of their careers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;People Operations Specialist, EMEA&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Global People Operations team on an 11-month FTC basis. This role is a critical pillar of Global People Operations, focusing on complex operational challenges and continuous improvement across the employee lifecycle. You will serve as a critical operational stakeholder enabling HR transformation by ensuring seamless support, optimizing processes with data-driven insights, and collaborating closely with our Centers of Excellence (COEs).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a proactive, data-driven, and systems-oriented member of the Global People Operations team, you will play a central role in maintaining an accurate HR operations infrastructure, facilitating critical employee lifecycle processes, and driving operational excellence to further delight our employees and partners. You will bridge operations and strategy, translating service insights into actionable improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elevated Employee Support (Tier 2 Escalation): &lt;/strong&gt;Provide a seamless and delightful support experience for Stripe employees and cross-functional partners, specifically handling complex inquiries and escalations routed from our Tier 1 Centralized Operations team or business partner teams, including bulk transaction processing, complex reorganization events, and separations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Optimization and Data-Driven Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;: Bring innovative, data-driven ideas and recommend enhancements to existing HR processes and workflows. Interpret data (e.g., case volumes, resolution times) and formulate insights to proactively drive continuous operational improvements that enhance the overall employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Transformation and Program Delivery: &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as a key operational stakeholder and contributor to significant HR transformation initiatives, major system updates, and the delivery of critical, ongoing HR programs across the employee lifecycle (e.g., onboarding, global mobility, offboarding).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder and COE Partnership: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with cross-functional teams and Centers of Excellence (COEs), including Compensation, Benefits, Employment Legal, and Employee Relations, to ensure operational needs are met, processes align, and smooth handoffs occur across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HRIS Management and Integrity: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain the accuracy and integrity of our HR Information System (Workday) by accurately entering employee change transactions manually and through bulk data uploads, ensuring a robust and reliable foundation for all HR data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Testing and Documentation: &lt;/strong&gt;Participate in end-to-end, user acceptance, and other testing of new/existing processes or workflows. Create and update Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) that document workflows from end to end, encompassing all system interactions and cross-functional handoffs for clarity and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Oversight: &lt;/strong&gt;Assist with vendor oversight and management for operational services related to your areas of expertise, ensuring service level agreements (SLAs) are met and performance standards are maintained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navigating Ambiguity: &lt;/strong&gt;Operate effectively in ambiguous situations using your technical expertise, Stripe’s operating principles, and stakeholder perspectives to determine the best course of action and communicate clearly about systemic blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in Human Resources or People Operations, with a focus on operational delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of HR processes, policies, and best practices across the employee lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical aptitude and proficiency with Workday (specifically data accuracy and management) and experience with Salesforce or a similar ticketing system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated problem-solving skills and the ability to handle complex Tier 2 escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving operational improvements and contributing to significant program delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience collaborating effectively with COEs (e.g., Legal, ER, People Partners) to resolve complex employee issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Written and verbal English communication skills focused on providing customer service and distilling complex information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration skills, with the ability to work cross-functionally and cross-culturally in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented, with a focus on accuracy, quality, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate ambiguity effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluency with the ability to interpret data and formulate insights to drive improvements and measure program success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Fluency: Knowledge and application of AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with knowledge management systems (e.g. Confluence).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and project management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team is made up of several groups that define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of Stripe&#39;s products. Product Designers work directly with Engineers, Product Managers, Data Scientists, and Marketers, as strategic partners, in each product area. In close collaboration with product teams, they shape user experiences, then translate them into high-quality designs that can be tested, shipped, and refined. Designers are responsible for building elegant, functional products that users love—and want to tell others about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global design team crafts product experiences that make cross-border selling as simple, performant, and scalable as domestic sales. Experiences empower businesses to easily expand into new markets worldwide without the friction of complex global operations, ranging from localized checkout experiences and comprehensive payment method coverage to handling global tax compliance and cross-border money management. Because of its global reach, this team&#39;s efforts drive significant impact for our users and business and navigate the unique challenges of designing for regions with dozens of currencies, languages, and regulatory frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product designer, you&#39;ll work closely with product managers and engineering teams to envision features in the Stripe Dashboard and checkout surfaces and partner with go-to-market teams to bring them to users. That includes new feature development, localization for priority geographies across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa, and setting vision for our products to meet new user expectations in an increasingly globally connected and AI-driven world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user workflows and pain points, and produce, test, and iterate on high-quality designs to solve user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, engineering, marketing, and strategy partners to define a north star and product experience for new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype user experiences for user research testing and internal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teams across Stripe to craft a seamless dashboard user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct UXR to test design decisions before shipping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our design systems teams to leverage and improve templates and components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of relevant design experience at a product-driven tech company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong craft demonstrated through a portfolio of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated skills in prototyping at high fidelity using the latest AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills through design deliverables, videos, and written artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a growth team driving user activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about building collaborative relationships with many partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for turning complexity into usable, beautiful experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong design leader comfortable bringing your point of view to a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to grow the GDP of the internet, and we won&#39;t stop until we&#39;ve made it easy for any business anywhere to participate in the digital economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Governments around the world are fundamentally changing how businesses report and exchange transactions. Continuous Transaction Controls (CTC) and e-invoicing mandates — now active or imminent in France, Germany, Spain, Poland, and across Latin America — require businesses to transmit structured invoice data through certified government networks in real time. For Stripe&#39;s global user base, compliant e-invoicing is rapidly becoming a prerequisite for conducting commerce, not a nice-to-have.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building the e-invoicing infrastructure that makes this invisible for Stripe users. That means embedding compliant invoice generation, validation, and transmission directly into Stripe Billing and Invoicing — abstracting the full complexity of regional mandates and network certification behind a seamless product experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, greenfield role. You&#39;ll own Stripe&#39;s e-invoicing product end-to-end: setting the strategy, driving execution, and making Stripe the go-to solution for businesses navigating the global shift to real-time invoicing compliance. You&#39;ll work at the intersection of product, engineering, partnerships, and go-to-market — and you&#39;ll be laying the foundation for a capability that will matter to every Stripe user operating in a mandated market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the e-invoicing product vision and roadmap, translating complex and evolving regulatory requirements into a coherent multi-year strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Stripe&#39;s expansion across mandated global markets (France, Germany, Spain, Poland) and into Latin America, sequencing coverage pragmatically against enforcement timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead build, buy, and partner decisions — evaluating the right combination of internal investment and external capabilities to meet compliance deadlines without sacrificing long-term product quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the end-to-end user journey: from onboarding (including business identity verification) to live invoice transmission via certified networks like Peppol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Billing, Invoicing, Tax, and Connect teams to embed e-invoicing as a native part of Stripe&#39;s financial infrastructure — not a bolted-on feature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish quality, reliability, and activation metrics that hold every component of the e-invoicing stack accountable, and use those metrics to drive continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM, Sales, and Solutions Engineering to position Stripe as the leading e-invoicing solution for upmarket and enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe credibly with regulators, certification bodies, and industry partners as we build direct relationships with key tax authorities and networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience, with at least 2 years in a B2B fintech, payments, tax, or compliance-adjacent product domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with the e-invoicing landscape — you understand CTC frameworks, structured invoice formats (Factur-X, XRechnung, PEPPOL BIS), and the regulatory dynamics driving mandates in Europe and Latin America&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency: you can credibly partner with engineers on API design, data schemas, and network integration architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to run a build/buy/partner analysis and translate the output into concrete roadmap decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching products across multiple markets simultaneously, including navigating localization, regulatory compliance, and differing user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional leadership — you get things done across Engineering, Legal, Finance, and GTM without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, direct communication: you can distill a complex compliance landscape into a compelling product narrative for both internal stakeholders and external audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating third-party technology providers or acquisitions into a core product platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe Billing, Invoicing, or Tax products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience building toward Peppol access point certification or direct integrations with national tax authority platforms (e.g., Chorus Pro, KSeF)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to B2B invoicing workflows in mid-market or enterprise contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role, why now&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;E-invoicing is one of the most consequential shifts in global business compliance in a decade, and Stripe is early in building the infrastructure to make it effortless. You&#39;ll have the mandate, the resources, and the cross-functional backing to build something significant — and the chance to make Stripe synonymous with world-class e-invoicing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is an equal opportunity employer. We look for people with exceptional abilities, who are excited by hard problems and big opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The payments landscape is changing rapidly and our team is at the forefront of this change. Depending on where you live, you may be used to paying with a credit card or bank direct debit (United States), iDEAL (Netherlands) or UPI (India), amongst hundreds of other global payment methods. It turns out how you pay is increasingly dependent on where you are and what business you&#39;re buying from.&lt;br&gt;The Core Payments team makes it easy for businesses global and domestic to offer familiar local payment experiences wherever their customers choose to pay. We build bank payment methods and local payment experiences, alongside the capabilities that make these methods easier to discover, integrate, and use across Stripe. Responsible for building Stripe&#39;s payment platform that allows us to build and distribute payment methods at scale. The team works across product, engineering, design, data science, partnerships, risk, and go-to-market teams to help businesses offer locally relevant payment experiences at global scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager, you’ll own relationships with some of the world’s largest payment providers and build products that drive billions in payment volume growth. You’ll help merchants offer locally relevant payment methods online and in person, improve payment performance, and expand acceptance across borders and into use cases such as recurring and agentic payments.&lt;br&gt;You’ll work directly with merchants to understand their payment needs, then partner with partnership managers and Stripe’s and financial partners’ product and engineering teams to define joint roadmaps and ship solutions. You’ll prioritize investments that grow adoption and improve approval rates while balancing revenue, margins, cost, and risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product vision and multi-quarter roadmap for a portfolio of strategic payment methods, using merchant feedback, partner capabilities, payment data, and market trends to set priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with merchants and financial partners to identify gaps in payment workflows and translate them into product requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build joint roadmaps with partnership managers and partners’ product and engineering teams, securing alignment on investments and resolving competing priorities and dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the case for new investments and work with engineering teams to ship improvements, balancing adoption, approval rates, revenue, margins, cost, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow payment method adoption with go-to-market teams by expanding cross-border acceptance and supporting use cases such as recurring and agentic payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Risk, Legal, and Compliance to implement controls and enforcement strategies that protect Stripe and financial partners while maximizing approval rates and minimizing losses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product marketing and go-to-market teams to turn roadmap priorities into clear launch and adoption plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become the product expert for your payment partners, providing insights and support to help them succeed on Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in building, launching, and scaling products that deliver meaningful user and business results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently defining product strategy and executing multi-quarter roadmaps, bringing clarity and direction to ambiguous problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional leadership, with the ability to influence product outcome, navigate competing interests, and drive decisions across teams and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on products that require aligning multiple stakeholders, developing joint roadmaps, and navigating competing priorities between internal goals and external partner objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering closely with engineers, designers, and external partners to build products and complex systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a knack for precise and concise articulation of user problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical capabilities with experience defining and tracking success metrics, running experiments (e.g., holdback tests), and using data to measure product impact on revenue, conversion, and margins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep user empathy and sound product judgment, with experience translating complex user needs into intuitive experiences and technical capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a dynamic and fast-paced environment with significant autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and comfort with complex ecosystem and platform-level problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with bank payments, online, local and instore payments methods with deep understanding of the conversion, costs, and risk trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with financial partners navigating risk, legal, and compliance requirements and users from various geographies and cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platform products and driving product adoption across multiple markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support Technologies builds the products, platforms, and capabilities behind Stripe’s support experiences. The team helps users resolve issues quickly, supports internal teams, and creates reusable technology that improves support across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role focuses on the complex support needs of Platforms and Connect. Platforms, connected accounts, and their customers each have different relationships with Stripe, access levels, and responsibilities. Resolving an issue often requires understanding who owns the account, which permissions apply, how products are configured, and which party should provide support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is building the foundations for more contextual support across this multi-party ecosystem. A key part of the work is improving Stripe’s customer-facing AI agent so it can understand these relationships, handle complex cases, and provide accurate, personalized resolutions at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;As a Product Manager for Support Experience, you will be responsible for improving the outcomes of Stripe’s user-facing&amp;nbsp;AI agent that holds 100k+ conversations per week.&amp;nbsp;You’ll be at the forefront of applied AI, solving problems for businesses and consumers, and redefining what great can look&amp;nbsp;like.&amp;nbsp;You’ll directly build agent capabilities to solve real-world user problems. That means getting hands-on with prompts,&amp;nbsp;evals, skills, tools and the machinery that lets you introspect and identify opportunities within the conversational&amp;nbsp;experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the product strategy and roadmap for Support Technologies serving Platform and Connect use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a deep understanding of the needs of platform operators, connected accounts, Stripe support teams, and platform support teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the capabilities and effectiveness of Stripe’s user-facing AI agent for Platform and Connect support experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring support problems and translate them into reusable product, platform, and AI agent capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, ship, and iterate on the prompts, skills, tools, and evaluations that enable the AI agent to solve real-world user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve how account relationships, roles, permissions, product configurations, and support history inform routing and resolution across AI and human-assisted support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tools that help the AI agent and support teams understand complex Platform and Connect issues and take the right next action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable platforms to support their connected accounts more effectively through appropriate tooling, visibility, automation, and contextual guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help clarify whether Stripe, the platform, or another party is responsible for resolving a user’s issue, and route the issue accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create continuous improvement loops that turn insights from AI agent conversations and support interactions into scaled solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Platform, Connect, and conversational AI product teams to incorporate support capabilities into critical product journeys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience, excluding internships and co-ops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep user empathy and a high bar for user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-team initiatives from ideation through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading technical products or a background in computer science or a similar field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team represents Stripe to governments, regulators, industry partners, and broader stakeholder audiences. We help the company understand and adapt to a changing global policy environment, anticipate and respond to challenges, and advocate for the needs of our users and the online economy. The team works closely with Policy Strategy, Legal, Communications, Marketing, and regional product and go-to-market teams to ensure coordinated, consistent engagement worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for a Public Affairs Campaigns Lead to build our profile in the policy landscape across EMEA, with a particular focus on the EU, its Member States, and the UK. Working closely with colleagues in Government Relations, Communications and Marketing, you will help turn Stripe’s policy priorities into compelling campaigns, develop thought leadership, and deliver policy events that reach the right audiences and shape the conversation. This person will be a truly great campaigns operative, someone willing to roll up their sleeves and who prides themselves on executing with excellence. You will help make Stripe’s ideas and expertise, and our users’ experiences, more visible and impactful - building a distinctive, credible voice for Stripe among policymakers and the wider policy community. If you are up for the challenge, we would love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Help develop and deliver public affairs campaigns that advance Stripe’s policy priorities across EMEA, taking campaigns from idea to execution, with clear objectives, target audiences, messages and tactics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop thought leadership that shapes the debate, including distinctive reports, commentary and campaign content that draws on Stripe’s expertise, data and users’ experiences.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Deliver policy events with lasting impact, putting Stripe and our users in front of those who create the policy landscape.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work with Government Relations and Policy Strategy colleagues to translate complex issues into compelling narratives and campaign materials that give policymakers a reason to pay attention.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bring the right channels and partners together to extend campaigns’ reach and influence, working with Government Relations colleagues as well as&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Communications, Marketing, industry groups, think tanks and users.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build Stripe’s policy brand by connecting individual campaigns, publications and events into a recognisable, credible voice in the region’s policy conversations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Contribute to the development of Stripe’s global public affairs campaigns capability, working closely with Public Affairs colleagues in the US and across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Minimum 3+ years of experience in public policy, public affairs, campaigning, government relations, communications, advocacy, or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience executing political or advocacy campaigns, building coalitions, coordinating stakeholders, and delivering events with impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Excellence in execution, someone able to move at speed to deliver incredible events, compelling content and impactful campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A terrific communicator and writer, fluent in English and adept at producing compelling thought leadership and campaign materials, clear briefings and impactful short-form messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Interest in and understanding of policy, government affairs, and the tech and/or payments ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Comfortable working with cross-functional partners and in an international environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proven collaborator who is resourceful, execution-oriented, and able to work both independently and as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Willingness to travel frequently for meetings and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Passionate about Stripe’s mission of helping ambitious businesses grow and thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Empathy, humility, and some comedy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Professional experience and existing relationships within the EU and/or UK policy and public affairs ecosystems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience supporting global or multi‑jurisdictional public affairs campaigns, including adapting and deploying global messaging and playbooks for local audiences.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Background or advocacy in technology, financial services, or related sectors.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Language skills beyond English are an advantage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to shape global public affairs campaigns and programmes at a fast-growing company touching millions of businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, mission-driven Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team that works closely with Policy Strategy, Legal, Communications, and Marketing around the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for professional growth and to take on increasing responsibility across global programmes.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual salary range for this role in London is £91,200 to £136,800.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Renewals Team is a strategic partner to Stripe&#39;s Sales organization, helping Stripe retain and expand revenue from its portfolio of existing users. We bring analytical rigor, commercial judgment, and operational discipline to the renewal process so account teams can navigate complex decisions with clarity, accuracy, and speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work closely with Sales, Deal Pricing, Deal Strategy, Customer Success and other cross-functional partners throughout the renewal lifecycle. The team analyzes account performance and contractual history, builds renewal scenarios, and develops recommendations that inform deal strategy and negotiation planning led by Account Executives. We also improve the systems and processes that enable Stripe to manage renewals at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Renewals Specialist, you will partner with account teams and cross-functional stakeholders to protect and grow Stripe&#39;s revenue. This is an analytical role at its core. You will combine quantitative analysis and financial modeling with user context to assess renewal options, identify risks and opportunities, and help teams make well-supported commercial decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on large, complex renewals, balancing the needs of Stripe and our users while helping account teams move deals forward on schedule. Success requires strong judgment, attention to detail, and the ability to build trusted relationships across teams. You should be comfortable operating in ambiguity, respectfully challenging assumptions, and engaging in constructive debate to reach better outcomes. You will also help design scalable processes so the team can handle fluctuating volumes while maintaining a high standard of operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives to develop and execute strategies for retaining and expanding revenue from existing users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a portfolio of upcoming renewals, tracking milestones, risks, dependencies, and stakeholder actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze historical pricing, product usage, account performance, and contractual terms to develop renewal recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build financial models and renewal scenarios that clarify commercial tradeoffs and support data-driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner on deal strategy and negotiation planning for large or complex renewals, providing analysis and a clear point of view to support commercial negotiations led by Account Executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify retention risks, expansion opportunities, and changes in user needs by combining feedback from Sales and Customer Success with account-level data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support accurate, timely quote and proposal development with account teams and cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships across Sales, Customer Success, Deal Pricing, Deal Strategy, and the technical and operational teams involved in the renewal lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on renewal performance, risks, and recommendations through clear weekly, monthly, and quarterly updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement scalable improvements to renewal workflows through tooling, automation, and the responsible use of AI-assisted solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a team culture grounded in ownership, integrity, intellectual honesty, and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in renewals, strategic account management, sales, customer success, or a related field, ideally in a high-growth technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and critical-thinking skills, including proficiency in Excel or Google Sheets and experience building financial models, pricing analyses, or business cases that turn complex data into clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound business judgment, with the ability to weigh competing priorities, risks, and tradeoffs in ambiguous situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build trust and influence partners without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to collaborate across functions while constructively challenging assumptions and helping teams reach sound decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time-management skills, with demonstrated experience prioritizing multiple time-sensitive workstreams, meeting deadlines, maintaining accuracy, and improving the processes that support the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial services, or FinTech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with contract renewals, pricing discussions, or complex deal structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with recurring-revenue or consumption-based business models, and with CRM, quoting, or business-intelligence tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using AI-assisted tools to accelerate research, analysis, documentation, and process improvement, with sound judgment around accuracy and appropriate data handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Crimes team plays a critical role in ensuring a healthy financial ecosystem and maintaining trust in Stripe&#39;s platform. We ensure that prohibited parties cannot utilize our services and identify bad actors engaging in money laundering, terrorist financing, or other financial crimes. As Stripe&#39;s user base and global footprint grow dramatically, this team is essential for mitigating risk and upholding regulatory compliance, directly contributing to Stripe&#39;s mission of increasing the GDP of the internet safely and responsibly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Risk Operations Analyst, you&#39;ll work to ensure our policies, operations, and workflows align with the needs of our financial partners. You&#39;ll be accountable for workflows impacting a variety of cross-functional internal and external stakeholders to identify and assess regulatory, contractual, and partner risk. Further, you&#39;ll influence and advise operational teams in building out scalable operational processes to ensure compliance with service level agreements, routine reporting, and overall risk mitigation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Demonstrate sound judgment and an ability to navigate non-binary, high-risk decisions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Adhere closely to process while still constantly questioning assumptions, suggesting improvements, and balancing user experience with compliance requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Effectively and clearly communicate with other Stripes, Stripe&#39;s users, and Stripe&#39;s financial partners • Identify and assess financial crime risks, conduct reviews using data analysis, and monitor for suspicious activity and trends&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Facilitate the redesign of business processes including clarifying, identifying issues, and facilitating changes to attain the highest levels of efficiency, control, and compliance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Help build and scale processes across the financial crimes operations ecosystem&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Identify gaps in current systems, policies, and strategies, and recommend enhancements and process improvements to mitigate emerging risks through a collaborative approach with stakeholders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 8+ years of experience in risk management, compliance, or financial operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Understanding of FinCrime red flags, its typologies, and how they can be identified&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience in developing and implementing process improvements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Demonstrates reasoned logic in decision-making and judgment, considers external and internal factors, and recommends solutions in complex situations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Effective communication skills with the ability to produce clear, precise, and concise written and presentation materials&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Ability to analyze feedback patterns and use these insights to drive process and product improvements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Policy development and regulatory knowledge—proven track record developing compliance policies and procedures for payment processing environments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Risk assessment—experience conducting merchant risk assessments, transaction monitoring, and implementing risk-based compliance controls&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Operational management and scaled operations—experience driving operational outcomes and managing large-scale operations through vendor partnerships, third-party integrations, and automated solutions to achieve efficiency and scalability in compliance processes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Data analysis tools such as SQL&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience in transaction monitoring or financial investigations, Sanctions, AML, EDD, KYC, and KYB&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Knowledge of payment processing systems and associated risks&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk Partnerships team is an essential part of Stripe’s Global Partnerships organization. Our team is responsible for building and maintaining relationships with key partner banks to manage risk for Stripe’s business activities. These banking partnerships are essential to enable Stripe to accept and make payments, provide credit, move &amp;amp; store money and develop new products and solutions to meet our users’ needs. We work across a broad range of risk and compliance topics including; credit, fraud, regulatory, financial crime, reputational, product and operational risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a new team member to collaborate with key banking partners throughout the UK, Europe and Stripe’s global partner network. These partners will work with Stripe to develop and deliver solutions that will build our Global Payments and Treasury Network. This role will support Stripe&#39;s goals to enable users to send and receive payments domestically and internationally, store funds securely, earn yield on those funds, and enable multi-currency fund flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk management is essential for managing these relationships, and this role requires a broad understanding of risk disciplines across banking activities, including accepting and making payments, money storage &amp;amp; transmission, and multi-currency/cross border fund flow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will lead activities to enhance risk management interactions between Stripe and its partners, manage key aspects of the partner relationships, and execute high-impact initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will work closely with key internal and external stakeholders to set objectives, coordinate priorities and drive execution. Internally, this role will coordinate closely with product and engineering teams, and cross-functional stakeholders including Risk, Fraud, Financial Crime &amp;amp; Supportability, Operations, Legal and Finance. Externally, this role will work closely with Partners&#39; Risk &amp;amp; Compliance teams, including senior management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead risk-focused initiatives in collaboration with global financial partners (banks, networks, payment methods) to:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster new business opportunities and user verticals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate on shared risk methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain compliance with agreed risk appetites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and maintain the health of relationships with key risk counterparts at partner banks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage projects and initiatives that support strong partner relationships regarding risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver business and policy recommendations that inform our risk posture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a representative and negotiator of our risk approach to banking partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance existing and develop new partner-facing risk management capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead risk-related partnership and product discussions with banking partners to align on risk approaches and strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and pursue business opportunities by creating innovative risk-aware solutions that expand our product and user base through banking partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years experience in risk-related role at a bank or fintech with experience of products &amp;amp; services that enabled users to send and receive payments domestically and internationally, store funds securely, earn yield on those funds, and enable multi-currency fund flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated deep knowledge and experience of working with bank payment schemes and networks (e.g. FPS, BACs, SEPA, ACH and local equivalents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep knowledge of risk and compliance issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to represent Stripe on risk, compliance, and product issues with banking partners to maintain positive relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, planning, and communication skills (written and verbal) to drive understanding, collaboration, and issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and a partnership mindset focused on improving processes and scaling solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-hand experience in risk management at a bank or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills, including navigating difficult situations, negotiating timelines, and influencing stakeholders across organizations and borders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and proactive, with the ability to thrive in uncertain and ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of financial crime programmes including; KYC/B, AML, Sanctions and Terrorist Financing, with a practical knowledge of the Bank Secrecy Act and Anti-Money Laundering regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of domestic &amp;amp; international payment schemes (e.g. FPS, CHAPS, BACs, SEPA, ACH, Wire).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the complex risks that are present when managing crossborder payments, including the management of high risk sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market experience across UK &amp;amp; Europe, with an understanding of how current and future regulations will impact Stripe and it’s banking partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of leveraging technology to support the development and embedment of scalable risk and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, we&#39;re building a financial system for the internet. We&#39;re hiring talented people like you to help us make this vision a reality.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sales Compensation team at Stripe is responsible for the overall compensation strategy, design, and payment administration for the global sales organization. We ensure that our objectives align with the compensation program and that our sales teams are paid accurately and on time. We provide thought leadership for the go-to-market initiatives so that performance and compensation are effectively correlated. The Sales Compensation team partners closely with the revenue-generating and support functions across Stripe to support the success of our sales efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re a key contributor to the sales compensation program design, implementation, and performance assessment of the sales organization. You&#39;ll have high visibility across multiple channels, owning the performance-to-compensation structure for specific sales teams and serving as the subject matter expert for strategic advice and implementation of any compensation programs (including SPIFFs and MBOs) that further align the sales focus with our OKRs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re passionate about sales compensation and comfortable working in ambiguous situations to identify optimal solutions for our sales teams to succeed. You have experience working across all levels and functions of an organization (preferably in a high-growth environment) to align our priorities with our sales team&#39;s motivation. You bring resilience and the ability to both partner and lead in cross-functional situations. You use analytics and quantitative data to support and evaluate decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the annual sales compensation plan design cycle for specific sales teams, including obtaining input and stakeholder approval for the proposed compensation structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement metrics for the plans that are specific, measurable, and align with company priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the rollout and enablement of the compensation plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct frequent quantitative measurement of the compensation plan effectiveness and apply learnings to the annual plan design process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose, evaluate, design, and measure the effectiveness of SPIFFs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the main contact for sales leadership to correlate objectives and compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own, update, and lead the enablement of the sales compensation resources for the sales organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own, update, and lead the enablement of the annual sales credit policies for the sales organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the sales compensation impacts in company strategy discussions (e.g., with Product)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have an in-depth understanding of the sales function, product priorities, and individual sales team characteristics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the commission calculation close process as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS or BA in Business, Finance, Economics, Math, or Statistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least five years of experience in a sales compensation role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least two years as a key point of contact with senior Sales, Finance, and HR leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least three years leading the sales compensation design process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Customer Relationship Management (CRM) (e.g., Salesforce) and Incentive Compensation Management (ICM) (e.g., Captivate IQ, Varicent, Xactly) tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with reporting tools and Tableau&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong logic, problem-solving, and Excel modeling skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very organized and attentive to detail, with excellent prioritization skills that allow you to consistently deliver quality results on time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high-growth, performance-focused environments and administering complex programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to forge strong bonds, work collaboratively with, and influence internal partners such as other Sales channels, Finance, and Business Applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI tools to enhance impact and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Sales or Sales Operations roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL programming experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

