&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement. &lt;/span&gt;An ideal candidate should have experience working for medium to large&amp;nbsp; software companies (preferably in In payment-tech), focused on identifying business priorities, technology strategy, and solution design.They will have demonstrated the ability to become a trusted advisor to senior executives and facilitate customer success including business value identification(discovery/ demo cycles), road mapping, as well as advising and defining successful execution strategies.&amp;nbsp;Ideal candidates have external customer-facing experience, have payment expertise (preferred but not required) who can present and architect Stripe’s solutions, and persuade decision makers to leverage Stripe technology to drive business value. Candidates have previous experience in web architecture, enterprise architecture or experience defining and optimizing financial business processes.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a similar customer-facing engineering role (e.g. solutions architect, sales engineer, customer success, professional services delivery) for a fin-tech/payment-tech / global software enterprise with 5+ years of total relevant experience (software development, enterprise sales/ architecture, business development etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a customer facing roles - presenting and architecting solutions. Domain experience in the payments space is preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding or background in writing code in at least 2 of Stripe’s primary deployment languages (Ruby, Python, JavaScript, Java, Go, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding oral and written communication skills, presentation skills, and comfortable explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able and willing to learn Stripe solutions (Payments, Billing, Connect, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability&amp;nbsp; to understand how a wide variety of technologies and systems interact with each other (ERP, CRM, Billing, Tax, Legacy)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational/time management skills and the ability to juggle competing priorities while working with multiple opportunities and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills to work seamlessly with the broader GTM team to support our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience solving open ended business problems with a combination of technology and creative thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel per business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Developer Productivity group is responsible for making Stripe’s developers happy and productive. We work on tools, processes, and code refactoring to accelerate Stripe engineering as Stripe scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people with an interest in building the tools to improve the day to day experience of Engineers in Stripe. The ideal candidate will have a passion for solving developer experience problems, and a pragmatic ability to ship results iteratively—powered by a mix of technical expertise across some or all of: language processing tools; version control systems; build systems; and distributed systems engineering. You’ll be working on a mix of engineer-facing systems, CI infrastructure platforms, and big-data engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a ton of important work to do, which is why we’re hiring! Our active projects change all the time, but here are a few examples of recent projects so you can get an idea of the types of work we do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage systems to handle CI at massive scale—including batching, speculative stacking, merge-race inhibition, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage systems to handle our enormous CI test suite–identifying and managing flaky tests, assessing and reproducing flakiness, and optimizing for test effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance our CI systems for reliability, including adaptive response to available capacity, resilience and self-recovery from outages, and highly-leveraged observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detect and isolate code breakages to minimize their blast radius.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with product engineers to understand and deliver their productivity needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and lead large technical projects with enormous impact for engineers within Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain the core CI systems used by all of Stripe’s engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrutinize and reason clearly about the technology and architecture choices we make in building these products. In many cases, you will be the owner of these decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly contribute to core interface design and write code. Serve as a role model for how great software should be written for Stripe as a whole.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arbitrate critical decisions correctly that fully consider software best practices, Stripe system realities, and numerous stakeholders’ preferences and concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach and mentor the next generation of technical leaders at Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the effective and highly-leveraged use of AI-assisted implementation, ops, and delivery within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional hands-on software development experience&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience designing and building large scale distributed systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of technically mentoring junior and senior engineers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer obsession, ability to articulate and represent customer experience in various forums to drive the right outcome&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability of defining &amp;amp; driving complex initiatives/projects across multiple teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success with cross-discipline and cross-team collaborations, possess strong conviction and courage skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy, responsibility, and think of yourself as entrepreneurial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Related experience in the area of Developer Tooling, CI/CD or DevOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supportability sits at the vital intersection of platform safety, regulatory trust and merchant growth. Our mission is to ensure legitimate businesses can seamlessly onboard and thrive on Stripe, while proactively safeguarding the financial ecosystem from bad actors and high-risk activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Supportability Decisions team is a newly forming pillar anchored in our Dublin office. In this role, you will be the foundational technical lead establishing this capability in Dublin. Our mission is to accelerate Stripe’s global expansion by building the canonical Supportability Decision Layer; a stateful distributed platform that provides unified, real-time, and explainable risk determinations to unlock fast, compliant merchant onboarding and payment method expansion worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doing this at scale requires solving high-stakes risk challenges with precision. Deceptive merchant activity, such as transaction laundering, introduces significant threats as bad actors actively adapt to mask illicit and unsupported activities behind legitimate storefronts. Rather than relying on rigid, fragmented controls that create unnecessary friction for good users, our team builds the intelligent decision systems that systematically separate legitimate businesses from adversarial behavior, enabling Stripe to grow safely and aggressively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Backend Engineer and Technical Lead for Supportability Decisions, you will take ownership of defining and building this new space from the ground up. You will build systems that operate at the intersection of AI/ML, distributed data processing and real-time risk decisioning. You will tackle high-ambiguity technical challenges in an adversarial threat landscape, turning broad risk policies and operational needs into resilient, high-throughput backend services and stateful decision engines. As the technical anchor in Dublin, you will set architectural patterns, mentor engineers as the team scales from its initial members to ~7 ICs, and drive technical alignment with distributed partner teams globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical vision, system architecture and delivery of the canonical Supportability Decision Layer, establishing stateful, explainable decision APIs consumed across automated systems and human operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect decision aggregation and AI/ML orchestration pipelines, synthesizing upstream machine learning outputs, website intelligence, backsite detection, and agentic AI evaluations into unified, low-latency determinations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design high-throughput, low-latency distributed backend services that balance platform safety, regulatory compliance, and minimal friction for legitimate merchants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate ambiguous, zero-to-one problem spaces to define clean domain models, contracts and interfaces across transaction laundering detection, web-presence screening and Local Payment Method (LPM) support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build resilient, AI-assisted decision engines designed to withstand circumvention, ensuring systems maintain integrity against sophisticated bad actors who actively evolve their tactics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the technical lead and mentor for the Dublin engineering team, setting architectural patterns, conducting design reviews, and raising the technical bar as the team expands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering Managers, Product Managers, Risk Operations, and Data Science to translate strategic risk policy into scalable technical roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical alignment and system integrations across global partner teams, leveraging strong written design artifacts and asynchronous collaboration to ensure cohesive platform architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a technical leader who thrives in ambiguity, has deep distributed systems instincts, and is energized by building a critical platform that enables global merchant growth while safeguarding the financial ecosystem. If that sounds like you, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional backend software engineering experience building and maintaining complex distributed systems in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record as a technical lead or staff engineer driving multi-quarter technical initiatives from ambiguous requirements to production delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience designing durable, scalable APIs, data models, and backend architectures capable of processing mission-critical data with high reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and leadership skills with experience mentoring engineers, aligning cross-functional stakeholders, and driving technical consensus across distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in a modern backend language (such as Ruby, Java, Go, Python, or C++).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building systems in trust, safety, or risk domains where external bad actors actively evolve their tactics (e.g., transaction laundering, fraud, deceptive practices, or platform abuse).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience architecting workflow orchestration, policy evaluation, or decision platforms that balance robust risk evaluation with frictionless merchant onboarding and product access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with global payment ecosystems, Local Payment Methods (LPMs), financial partner dynamics, or card network standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in AI/ML systems, agentic workflows, orchestrators, or integrating machine learning models into high-throughput, real-time backend decision pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience serving as an anchor or founding engineer establishing a new team or technical domain in a regional engineering hub.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building the economic infrastructure for the internet. Millions of businesses use Stripe to accept payments, manage revenue, and grow globally. Stripe Tax helps businesses calculate, collect, and manage indirect taxes as they sell across products, markets, and business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Staff Product Manager to help shape the future of Stripe Tax. In this role, you will lead high-impact product strategy and execution across a broad portfolio, making it easier for businesses to understand, calculate, collect, and manage tax as they grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Manager on Stripe Tax, you will identify the most important opportunities to improve our tax products and turn them into focused strategies, durable platforms, and exceptional user experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Engineering, Design, Tax, Partnerships, Go-to-Market, and other product teams to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set strategy and lead product initiatives that help more businesses successfully adopt and use Stripe Tax.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the speed, accuracy, reliability, and usability of Stripe Tax calculations and related workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand support for the geographies, tax requirements, industries, products, and business models that matter most to Stripe users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build capabilities for complex tax needs, such as registrations, exemptions, address and fulfillment logic, tax customization, and other business-specific requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable products and platform capabilities that work across Stripe’s ecosystem, including integrations, connector apps, marketplaces, and Connect platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Stripe to create coherent end-to-end experiences spanning calculation, collection, reporting, and tax management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer insight, market context, data, and technical understanding to prioritize investments and make clear tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align senior stakeholders and cross-functional partners around a shared product direction, measurable outcomes, and an execution plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help make Stripe Tax a product businesses can rely on as they scale. Merchants should be able to confidently answer “yes” to questions such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can I use Stripe Tax for my business and the locations where I sell?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Does Stripe Tax support the taxes and business models that apply to me?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can it calculate tax accurately for my registrations, exemptions, customers, products, and fulfillment model?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is it fast, reliable, and easy for my team to operate?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Does it work with the other Stripe products, platforms, and integrations my business depends on?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a product leader who is comfortable operating in ambiguous, high-stakes spaces where customer needs, regulatory complexity, technical constraints, and commercial opportunity intersect. You can translate a broad mission into a focused strategy, build alignment across teams, and deliver meaningful products over multiple horizons.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You likely have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant product management experience, including ownership of complex, platform-oriented, or technically deep products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of setting strategy and delivering multi-team initiatives with measurable business and customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in prioritizing across customer needs, market opportunities, operational complexity, and engineering investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineering and design partners to build reliable, scalable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to communicate clearly with executive stakeholders and to align diverse partners around a shared direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about global commerce, financial infrastructure, tax, compliance, payments, marketplaces, or developer platforms. Direct domain experience is helpful but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-first mindset and the ability to turn complex requirements into simple, effective product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tax is a fundamental challenge for businesses that sell across borders, channels, and business models. Stripe Tax has the opportunity to remove that complexity, helping businesses launch faster, expand with confidence, and operate globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-leverage role at the intersection of global commerce, financial infrastructure, and product platform strategy. You will shape how Stripe Tax evolves to serve the next generation of internet businesses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abuse Control Engineering (ACE) is Stripe’s rapid-response technical defense and control incubator. When urgent abuse vectors emerge, ACE uses real-world attacker telemetry to prototype, test, and deploy software safeguards before vulnerabilities can be exploited at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We partner closely with Fraud, Risk, Abuse Research, and Product Engineering to run rigorous experiments that balance effective risk mitigation with legitimate user activity and conversion. Operating as both a strike team and an incubator, ACE builds automated regression suites to prevent threats from recurring and transfers mature controls to long-term product owners across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Abuse Control Engineer on the ACE team, you will design, prototype, and incubate technical defenses that safeguard Stripe’s financial ecosystem against complex, cross-cutting abuse vectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When emerging threat patterns reveal weaknesses in Stripe products, ACE rapidly builds and experiments with technical safeguards. Guided by empirical evidence and Stripe’s Fraud Taxonomy 3.0 (FT3) framework, you will translate threat intelligence into precise technical control requirements, such as API rate limits, step-up challenges, parameter validation, and pre-debit holds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will run experiments to evaluate risk reduction against the impact on legitimate user conversion, carefully balancing security and product velocity. You will manage controls through a structured incubation lifecycle, build automated regression suites to prevent threats from recurring, and partner with product engineering teams to transfer mature, long-term defenses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rapid control prototyping:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Design, prototype, and deploy technical controls across API, protocol, and product boundaries to address high-impact abuse vectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evidence-based technical requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Translate empirical attacker evidence and FT3 threat research from Abuse Research, Fraud, and Security teams into precise technical abuse requirements and control specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Control co-design:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Collaborate with teams across Stripe to design resilient, secure controls across payments, onboarding, identity, and Connect surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Run rigorous experiments and A/B tests to measure risk reduction against the impact on legitimate user conversion, optimizing controls to minimize friction while neutralizing threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regression testing:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build comprehensive regression test suites and automated attack simulations with Abuse Research to ensure mitigated abuse vectors do not recur.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Execute ACE’s incubation model by defining handoff criteria, operational documentation, timelines, and target dates for transferring successful controls to product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in security engineering, software engineering, application security, or anti-abuse engineering in a high-scale production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s or master’s degree in computer science, cybersecurity, software engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong software development background, with proficiency in Python, Go, Java, or a similar production programming language, as well as advanced SQL skills for analyzing system telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using frontier AI models for software development, learning, and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building API-level safeguards, rate-limiting frameworks, authentication or authorization checks, or input-validation controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automated testing frameworks, including writing unit, integration, and regression tests for critical backend software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration and communication skills, with a track record of partnering across security, product, and platform teams to drive technical outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of designing and executing A/B tests, evaluating control efficacy, and balancing security safeguards against user conversion friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in threat modeling, secure systems architecture, and modern application-security design principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with established threat frameworks, such as FT3 or MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK, and experience applying adversary kill-chain analysis to build resilient defenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of financial fraud vectors, threat-actor tactics, techniques, and procedures, and attacker infrastructure, including account takeover, card testing, and credential stuffing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with large-scale data-processing platforms, such as Databricks, Trino, or PySpark, to monitor and measure control performance across distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience incubating software features, establishing clear operational handoff criteria, and transitioning ownership to partner engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collecting and filing sales &amp;amp; indirect taxes is a classic area for technology disruption. Companies selling across countries, states, and even smaller jurisdictions have to navigate through a myriad of tax rates, product-level tax exemptions, filing requirements, and registration obligations. The rules are constantly changing, and not accurately calculating and filing tax can have legal ramifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s no surprise then that solving tax compliance is a top user request. We launched Stripe Tax as a new SaaS product in 2021 to make tax compliance as effortless as possible. The Stripe Tax team builds the systems and experiences that help businesses understand where they have obligations, calculate the right tax, and automate reporting and filing. We solve this at a global scale for users ranging from ambitious startups to the world’s largest enterprises, whose requirements demand exceptional correctness, extensibility, and operational rigor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced technical leader to shape the architecture and technical roadmap for Stripe Tax. You will work alongside leaders across engineering, product, design, operations, and go-to-market teams to turn complex and evolving tax requirements into simple, reliable experiences for millions of businesses. You will lead high-impact, multi-team efforts, make durable technical decisions, and raise the bar for how we build and operate Stripe Tax.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the technical strategy and execution for Stripe Tax’s most important and ambiguous product and platform investments, from early exploration through production adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work backwards from the needs of complex global businesses and evolving tax regulations to identify high-leverage opportunities and shape the product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, product, design, operations, legal, go-to-market, and infrastructure leaders to align teams and deliver cohesive tax experiences across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve scalable, resilient systems and data models that meet the exceptionally high standards for correctness, auditability, security, and availability required in tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive interoperability across Stripe products and external tax ecosystems, scrutinizing service boundaries, interfaces, and data contracts to keep the platform extensible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the engineering bar through hands-on technical leadership, clear decision-making frameworks, operational excellence, and mentorship that accelerates other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of industry software engineering experience building and operating large-scale, distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep software engineering expertise, with a track record of making sound architectural decisions while remaining hands-on in the code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading complex, multi-team technical programs from ambiguous problem definition through successful delivery and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to set long-term technical direction, identify the highest-leverage investments, and make progress amid uncertainty and competing constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and influence skills, with the ability to build alignment among senior technical, product, and business stakeholders without relying on authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to growing other engineers through mentorship, technical feedback, and a culture of rigorous, inclusive, and data-informed decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in tax, financial technology, payments, accounting, financial reporting, or another domain where correctness and regulatory complexity are central&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with large enterprise customers and translating their complex requirements into durable platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing robust integrations with external systems and APIs, or leading platform work that spans backend services, data, and user-facing experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategy &amp;amp; Analytics team in Internal Systems aspires to supercharge the wider Internal Systems and SDC organizations with analytics and insights. The Internal Systems and SDC org creates the engineering infrastructure and runs the internal operations that enables Stripe to succeed. Seller Systems, within this organization, builds the tools that help our sellers scale and sell our products. We deliver data-driven insights that inform business decisions, drive measurable operational improvements, and guide strategy. We are not just data analysts, we are a mix of strategic business partners, deeply strategic and/or technical operational executors. We ensure timely, reliable, high-quality data for not just Internal Systems and SDC, but for stakeholders across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll be the go-to expert for your business area. You’ll partner directly with product and engineering leaders within Seller Systems and be their go-to for all things data, insights, and strategy. You’ll be hands-on and responsible for delivering critical insights, ensuring data driven decision making is at the core of what we do. You’ll partner with leadership to drive product strategy, planning, goal-setting and performance tracking. You may also scope and lead mission critical projects and execute on strategic initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics &amp;amp; Insights: Wrangle large, highly complex datasets using SQL into actionable insights and become the data expert for your business area. Develop metrics and large-scale dashboards to track the health of our user-facing and internal teams. Perform analyses (using SQL &amp;amp; other analytical tools/languages), identify trends, conduct research, build models, all to deliver objective, critical insights that can inform leadership of opportunities, risks, and strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with executives: Create narratives and documents that tell the story of your business area to influence senior Product, Engineering and Sales leadership and Stripe executive team decision making. Own executive-facing weekly, monthly or quarterly reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management: Influence and drive cross-functional change by partnering with stakeholders across a wide internal network of globally distributed teams, including Ops, Finance, Data Science, Product/Engineering, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence: Design, optimize and drive operational reviews and rhythm of the business. Guide the planning and goal-setting process for your business area, as well as progress checks throughout the year. Bring and consistently apply a ROI lens to all operational decisions, so we can make better-informed trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct internal knowledge sharing sessions to strengthen the team&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re passionate about solving business problems and making a direct impact on business. You thrive in environments with many moving parts and quickly pick up new domain knowledge and technologies (e.g. AI). We’re seeking someone with excellent communication and advanced SQL/analytics abilities. Strong background in Sales Analytics or prior AI experience is highly preferred, though these can also be developed on the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in STEM major (i.e. Computer Science, Math, Stat, Engineering, etc.) and 4+ years of prior working experience in data analysis fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical ability, proficiency with SQL (minimum of 3 years advanced SQL) and strong understanding of data relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with extremely large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI tools (Claude Code, etc.) and have demonstrated measurable impact from AI in your role or in others’ around you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication, presentation skills &amp;amp; stakeholder management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in or with Sales and/or Operations organizations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise working cross-functionally and with globally distributed teams to drive business and operational goals using data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to connect the big picture to minute details, toggling between them to set and operationalize strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-paced environments (e.g. high-growth fintech/tech company, management consulting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Product Manager and Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with visualization tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metronome, now part of Stripe, is the leading usage-based billing platform built for modern software companies. With Metronome, companies can launch products faster, offer any pricing model, and streamline finance workflows without writing code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our platform computes millions of invoices per billing period and is scaling rapidly to accommodate new customers, saving them hours of development time and manual invoicing and enabling them to use consumption data to better serve their customers. Our customers love our product and approach, and we’re humbled to work with amazing companies like OpenAI, NVIDIA, Confluent, and Anthropic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of our technical support engineering team, you will be on the front lines providing world-class customer service. As part of our engineering organization, you will become an expert on our product and partner closely with Metronome&#39;s engineers, customer success, solutions architecture, and growth teams, as well as our customers&#39; developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary responsibilities will include handling customer escalations through our ticketing system, using internal observability tools to diagnose and scope customer-facing issues, collaborating directly with customers via Slack and other channels, and developing internal tools and documentation to improve the support experience. Since we view every support escalation as an opportunity to learn, both as individuals and as a company, you will play a critical role in providing feedback to our product team on common challenges and influencing our product roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through your interactions with individual customers, you will help improve our product for everyone. Your work will play a crucial role in ensuring our customers&#39; success and the continued effectiveness of their integration with Metronome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance to customers’ developers on best practices for integrating with our APIs and utilizing our functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot any issues that arise from customers and diagnose any blockers. Escalate issues with customer context to the engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop internal tools to automate customer workflows that are currently unavailable in our product. Provide feedback on recurring patterns and advocate for addressing feature gaps in the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and assist in implementing a comprehensive knowledge base to assist customers with using our product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of work experience in a B2B customer-facing technical support organization or in engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineering teams and providing technical feedback on customer issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to debug and triage bugs and escalations from customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can communicate technical capabilities of the product to customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing scripts or internal tools using APIs, and functional knowledge of SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to break down complex technical concepts clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset of customer empathy and ability to solve challenging problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an early or founding member of a support team, including building processes from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup experience and familiarity with scaling a support team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in one or more of Typescript, Python, or Ruby&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked on modern enterprise software which is business critical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating knowledge base articles and internal documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with at least one ticketing system, such as Pylon, Zendesk, Front, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;As one of the founding Startup Account Executives in EMEA, you’ll pioneer the adoption of safe, frontier AI across the region by securing strategic deals with some of the fastest growing technology companies in the world. You’ll leverage your consultative sales expertise to propel revenue growth while becoming a trusted partner to customers, helping them embed and deploy AI while uncovering its full range of capabilities. In collaboration with GTM, product, and marketing teams, you’ll build Anthropic&#39;s presence across EMEA&#39;s dynamic startup ecosystem, continuously refining our value proposition, sales methodology, and market positioning to ensure differentiated value across the landscape.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;The ideal candidate will have a passion for developing new market segments, pinpointing high-potential opportunities, and executing strategies to capture them. As an early member of our EMEA sales team, you&#39;ll help establish Anthropic&#39;s commercial foundation in the region while advancing the ethical development of AI technology.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win new business and drive revenue for Anthropic. Find your way to the right people at prospective customers, educate them about LLMs, and help them succeed with Anthropic. You’ll own the full sales cycle, from first outbound to launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute innovative sales strategies to meet and exceed revenue quotas. Analyze market landscapes, trends, and dynamics to translate high-level plans into targeted sales activities, partnerships, and campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead market expansion by pinpointing new customer segments and use cases, collaborating cross-functionally to differentiate our offerings and sustain a competitive edge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inform product roadmaps and features by gathering customer feedback and conveying market needs, providing insights that strengthen our value proposition and enhance the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define our regional GTM operations and sales methodologies by incorporating learnings into playbooks, templates, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You may be a good fit if you have:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical sales experience with a proven track record of driving adoption of emerging technologies with a consultative, solutions-oriented sales approach, preferably across EMEA markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity working within complex sales cycles, selling to technical stakeholders, and securing strategic deals by understanding multifaceted technical requirements and crafting tailored solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Success as a strategic business advisor, deeply understanding the needs of startup founders and creating innovative solutions that align with their vision and help them succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to negotiating complex, customized commercial agreements with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of exceeding quota by effectively qualifying and advancing opportunities in a fast-paced work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and the ability to present confidently and build connections across all customer levels, from ICs to C-level executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for bringing order to chaos and an enthusiastic “roll up your sleeves&#39;&#39; mentality. You are a true team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical approach to understanding customer needs combined with creative follow-up to advance opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for emerging technologies like AI, with interest in ensuring they are developed safely and responsibly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic, analytical approach to assessing markets combined with creative, tactical execution to capture opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for and/or experience with advanced AI systems. You feel strongly about ensuring frontier AI systems are developed safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deadline to apply:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;None. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€155.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€205.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For roles performing work in California: &lt;/strong&gt;We will consider for employment all qualified applicants, including those with arrest or conviction records or criminal histories, in a manner consistent with the requirements of applicable state and local laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the City of Los Angeles’ Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is growing quickly across EMEA, and we need recruiters who can help us hire exceptional people into the teams that keep the company running and bring our work to customers. We’re looking for a Recruiter to join our Talent team in London to own full-cycle recruiting for either our G&amp;amp;A functions (Finance, Legal, People, and related areas) and our Go-To-Market organization (Sales, Marketing, Partnerships, and Customer-facing roles), depending on business need and your background.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-cycle individual-contributor role for a strong recruiter who can run an excellent process end to end—sourcing, screening, managing stakeholders, and closing. You’ll partner with hiring managers across EMEA to understand what great looks like, build healthy pipelines, and deliver a candidate experience that reflects Anthropic’s values. You’ll work in a fast-moving environment where priorities shift, and you’ll have real ownership over the roles you run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re open to candidates whose strength is in G&amp;amp;A recruiting or in GTM recruiting; in your application, tell us where your experience is deepest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own full-cycle recruiting for a portfolio of G&amp;amp;A or GTM roles across EMEA—from intake through offer and close&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with hiring managers to scope roles, calibrate the bar, and build effective sourcing strategies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Source and engage high-quality active and passive candidates, building diverse and competitive pipelines&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run structured, rigorous, and candidate-centric interview processes that uphold Anthropic’s hiring bar&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage candidates through the process with clear communication and a great experience at every stage&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with the broader Talent team, People Partners, and Compensation to structure offers and guide candidates to close&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use data to track pipeline health and share insight that helps hiring managers make good decisions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience in either G&amp;amp;A (Finance, Legal, People) or GTM (Sales, Marketing, Partnerships) hiring&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track record of closing strong candidates in competitive markets&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with the EMEA talent landscape and comfort recruiting across multiple countries&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong stakeholder management—you build trust and partnership with hiring managers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent organization and the ability to manage multiple searches at once without dropping details&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clear, direct communication style and a bias toward action&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfort operating with ambiguity in a fast-moving environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Genuine interest in Anthropic’s mission and the role recruiting plays in achieving it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience recruiting at a high-growth technology, AI, or machine learning company&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience recruiting across both G&amp;amp;A and GTM functions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience hiring across multiple EMEA markets, including the UK and Ireland&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with Greenhouse or similar ATS platforms&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional European language skills relevant to hiring across the region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
