&lt;p&gt;MongoDB’s EMEA Marketing team is hiring a Demand Generation Lead to drive digital acquisition among AI-native startups and digital-native companies, while building scalable, centralized enterprise programs across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the EMEA Demand Programs Leader, you’ll create and run repeatable, integrated programs that generate engagement with target people and accounts, qualified leads, and pipeline, while supporting broader EMEA demand generation campaigns. Your primary focus will be AI-native companies and digital natives: fast-growing, developer-led organizations where MongoDB’s platform and startup programs are a strong fit. You’ll reach them through digital channels, founder and VC/PE community groups, and relevant events. This role blends strategy with hands-on execution: you’ll design programs, run them, and demonstrate their impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Dublin for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own integrated EMEA acquisition programs for AI-native and digital-native companies, reaching founders, technical leaders, and developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use intent signals, audience segmentation, and lead scoring to prioritize target companies and personas, and nurture technical champions toward sales-ready status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run structured experiments across channels, messaging, creative, and offers; scale what works, stop what doesn’t, and explore AI-enabled tactics and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the broader EMEA demand-generation plan by sharing channel insights and performance data, and running digital and demand campaigns for target enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable, centralized EMEA programs by identifying duplicated or similar country-level activity and replacing it with repeatable programs, templates, and playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional and country Marketing, Sales, Ecosystem, Global Marketing, Content, Developer Relations, Strategic Events, and Marketing Operations to connect programs to wider campaigns and secure assets, landing pages, and tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage budgets, agencies, forecasting, and spend efficiency; report on leads, MQLs, pipeline, cost per lead, and conversion; communicate recommendations to senior stakeholders; and document best practices for regional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;We’re looking for someone with&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in B2B technology marketing, including 3+ years in demand generation, digital marketing, or lead acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of running multi-country or regional programs and demonstrating pipeline impact, ROI, and cost efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience across digital channels, including paid search and social, email, content syndication, and web and landing-page optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and a metrics-driven approach to funnel reporting, attribution, and experiment design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketing technology such as Salesforce, a marketing automation platform (Marketo or similar), and intent or ABM tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project and budget management skills, the ability to prioritize competing demands, and experience building scalable programs and playbooks that local teams can adopt. You can influence senior stakeholders across regions, communicate effectively in written and spoken English, and bring ownership and initiative to a fast-moving environment. Additional European languages are an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: Experience marketing to AI-native companies, startups, digital natives, or developer audiences; applying AI tools to targeting, content, personalization, or optimization; or working with developer or product-led growth funnels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
