&lt;p&gt;The MongoDB Atlas team is a diverse group of contributors working together to help our users manage MongoDB at global scale. We are responsible for MongoDB Atlas: our database-as-a-service offering and fastest-growing product, which allows users to deploy fault-tolerant, globally distributed MongoDB clusters in just minutes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking an Engineering Manager to build and lead a new Atlas Identity and Access Management (IAM) in Dublin. This is a people-first leadership role: you will build the team, establish its culture and working cadence, and partner with product and engineering leadership to deliver on a high-visibility roadmap.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Dublin for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Role Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and grow a team of engineers in Dublin, establishing the team’s culture, practices, and ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own all aspects of people management: hiring, onboarding, coaching, career growth, performance management, and compensation planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Management, Program Management, and Engineering leadership to define the team’s roadmap and specify, prioritize, and deliver new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster technical excellence through design reviews, architecture guidance, and operational rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the team’s liaison to the broader IAM organization, collaborating across teams, sites, and time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With your team, own operational excellence for mission-critical identity services for Atlas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an environment where engineers can do the best work of their careers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across time zones with US-based IAM teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing a team of software engineers, including hiring, performance and growth management, compensation planning, and mentoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience developing backend systems (Java, Go, C#, C++, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or significantly scaling an engineering team; greenfield or new-site experience a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in backend and distributed systems; experience with security, identity, or access management a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High empathy, ownership, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams that collaborate across time zones a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Success Measures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In 1 month, you’ll have onboarded, met your team and stakeholders, and learned our software development lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In 3 months, you’ll have led members of your team to deliver customer-facing value in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In 6 months, you’ll be running a fully independent roadmap for your team, and fully owning the growth of your team and the operational excellence of your systems&lt;/li&gt;
