&lt;p&gt;Atlas Agent Engine is a platform that runs AI agents as customer workloads in strongly isolated environments, on multi-tenant Kubernetes clusters across multiple cloud providers. The platform&#39;s SRE team owns the operational foundations: the Kubernetes fleet, networking, observability and alerting, and tenant isolation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of an expanding SRE team, you will play a key role in defining operational strategies for our runtime, enhancing runtime security, and supporting expansion across additional cloud platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Dublin for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The ideal candidate should:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 6+ years of experience working on software development and operating distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Go, or a similar language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have operated Kubernetes in production and be comfortable debugging it below the abstraction: scheduling, cluster networking, and node-level issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Linux operating system internals and networking concepts (e.g., TCP/IP, DNS, TLS, routing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in cloud infrastructure platforms, including AWS, Google Cloud Platform (GCP), or Azure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Value efficiency in processes and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess a customer-focused mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and improve the multi-tenant Kubernetes infrastructure that runs customer workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build for reliability, making services and infrastructure available, resilient, fault-tolerant, and self-healing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and configure key metrics to detect incidents and quantify service health, availability, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in a 24/7 on-call rotation to resolve issues involving the platform infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Strong candidates may also have experience with&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes networking (e.g., Istio, Cilium) and service mesh or edge load balancing in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing secure, multi-tenant runtime environments at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and scaling infrastructure across multi-cloud environments (AWS, GCP, or Azure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Virtualization and workload isolation technologies&lt;/li&gt;
