&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SolarWinds is looking for a Principal Product Manager to own the end-to-end eCommerce experience. This includes the digital engine that converts prospects into customers and customers into advocates. This is a senior individual contributor role with high visibility across Product, Engineering, Finance, and Go-to-Market, and it carries real potential to grow into a people leadership position as the eCommerce function scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will define the vision and roadmap for how SolarWinds sells online which spans self-serve purchasing, pricing and packaging presentation, checkout and payment flows, trial-to-paid conversion, and subscription management. You’ll set strategy, influence the roadmap across adjacent product areas, and raise the bar for how SolarWinds thinks about digital revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the kind of role where your work is directly traceable to revenue. If you want ownership, strategic scope, and room to grow - this is it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;eCommerce Strategy &amp;amp; Vision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Define and own the multi-year product vision and roadmap for SolarWinds’ eCommerce capabilities, aligned to company revenue and growth objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Set the strategic framework for how SolarWinds sells online - spanning SMB self-serve, mid-market, and enterprise digital motions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Influence pricing, packaging, and go-to-market strategy in partnership with Product, Finance, and GTM leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Represent eCommerce at the executive level, translating complex product decisions into clear business impact narratives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-Serve &amp;amp; Product-Led Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Own the self-serve buying journey from trial activation through paid conversion and upsell, building frictionless experiences that drive revenue without requiring a sales touch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Define and optimize in-product upgrade and expansion paths that accelerate product-led growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Partner with Product and Engineering teams to build the in-app purchasing and entitlement infrastructure that powers self-serve revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Measure and improve key PLG metrics: trial conversion rate, time-to-value, activation rate, and self-serve ARR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Checkout, Pricing &amp;amp; Packaging Experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Own the end-to-end checkout experience: product catalogue, pricing pages, cart, payment, order confirmation, and post-purchase flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive pricing and packaging display strategy - ensuring the right offer is surfaced to the right buyer at the right moment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Partner with Finance and Legal on payment method expansion, tax and compliance requirements, and currency localization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Lead major platform investments such as commerce engine selection, payment infrastructure, and subscription management tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conversion Optimization &amp;amp; Analytics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Build and maintain a data-driven operating model for eCommerce performance, with clear KPIs and a test-and-learn culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Own funnel analytics: traffic-to-trial, trial-to-paid, cart abandonment, average order value, and lifetime value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive a structured A/B testing program across pricing pages, checkout flows, and upgrade prompts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Establish reporting and dashboards that give leadership clear visibility into digital revenue health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Influence &amp;amp; Organizational Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Operate as the connective tissue between Product, Engineering, Marketing, Sales, Finance, and Customer Success on all things eCommerce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive alignment on roadmap priorities without direct authority - you know how to lead through influence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Mentor and elevate other PMs on eCommerce thinking, customer journey analysis, and conversion-first product design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Build the playbooks, frameworks, and practices that scale the eCommerce function as the team grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 10+ years of product management experience, with a strong track record owning revenue-generating digital products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 3 - 5+ years of direct eCommerce, self-serve, or PLG experience in a B2B SaaS or hybrid (SaaS + on-prem) environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Proven ability to define and execute product strategy at the principal or senior staff level - setting vision, influencing roadmaps across teams, and driving major product decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Deep understanding of eCommerce fundamentals: checkout UX, payment infrastructure, pricing and packaging strategy, subscription lifecycle, and conversion optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong analytical skills - you are comfortable with funnel metrics, A/B test design, cohort analysis, and presenting performance data to executive stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Demonstrated ability to lead through influence in a matrixed organization, building alignment across Product, Engineering, GTM, Finance, and Legal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience with pricing and packaging strategy, including how to model and present trade-offs across tiers, bundles, and go-to-market motions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Excellent written and verbal communication skills - you can tell a clear story at the executive level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience mentoring other PMs and contributing to team-level craft and practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll Be a Great Fit If You…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Think in full customer journeys and have a natural instinct for removing friction from the buying experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Are equally comfortable in a spreadsheet modelling conversion scenarios as you are in a design review shaping checkout UX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Have strong opinions about what good eCommerce looks like - and can back them up with data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Thrive operating with high autonomy and aren’t waiting to be told what to build next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Are energized by the idea of building something from a strong foundation - there’s real room to make this function your own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Want a role that is IC today but keeps a clear path to leading a team as eCommerce grows.&lt;/p&gt;
