&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SolarWinds is hiring a Data Platform Engineer to own BigQuery platform administration, Dataplex-based data security, and end-to-end ELT integrity across the Enterprise Data stack. BigQuery, GCP, and Dataplex are the core depth this role brings, with Fivetran ingestion reliability and pipeline performance as a close second.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond keeping the platform reliable, this role is also expected to be a source of BigQuery best-practice guidance — helping the wider team get more out of the platform, and driving adoption of new BigQuery and GCP features where they improve performance, cost, or reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A core expectation is disciplined, auditable access administration: BigQuery and Dataplex govern PII and sensitive data across the platform, so this role&#39;s IAM and policy-tag work needs to hold up to governance and compliance scrutiny, done in partnership with the Data Governance and Cloud Security teams on standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT THIS ROLE OWNS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ingestion reliability — monitoring, triage, and troubleshooting for Fivetran connectors feeding BigQuery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BigQuery platform administration — IAM, service accounts, cost and performance management, project/dataset structure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BigQuery best practices and feature adoption — advising the team on patterns, performance, and cost, and evaluating new platform features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dataplex governance and security — user-level permissions, PII masking, and policy tag administration, executed in partnership with Data Governance (standards) and Cloud Security (access-control policy).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ELT pipeline integrity and performance — making sure data flows correctly and efficiently from ingestion through BigQuery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runbooks and operational hardening across the tools this role manages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ingestion &amp;amp; platform administration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor Fivetran connectors; investigate warnings, failures, delays, and abnormal load behaviour into BigQuery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer BigQuery — IAM, service-account patterns, dataset/project structure, cost visibility and optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full user lifecycle (onboarding, role changes, offboarding) for BigQuery and Dataplex access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BigQuery best practices &amp;amp; feature adoption&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise Data Engineering and Analytics teams on BigQuery best practices — partitioning, clustering, query optimisation, and cost management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track new BigQuery and GCP platform features and drive adoption where they improve reliability, performance, or cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain internal guidance and documentation on BigQuery patterns and standards for the wider team to follow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dataplex governance &amp;amp; security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer Dataplex policy tags and taxonomies for PII and sensitive-data masking at the column level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grant and audit user-level BigQuery/Dataplex access (Fine-Grained Reader, Masked Reader, and equivalent roles) against least-privilege principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Data Governance team, who set PII classification standards and policy-tag taxonomy; this role implements and administers the technical configuration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Cloud Security team on IAM and access-control standards, ensuring BigQuery/Dataplex configuration aligns with company-wide security policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ELT pipeline integrity &amp;amp; performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor data integrity and performance end to end, from Fivetran ingestion through BigQuery, catching completeness and freshness issues before they reach downstream consumers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor BigQuery job and query performance underlying downstream transformation and reporting, flagging issues to Data Engineering or Business Intelligence when the root cause sits in their layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident response &amp;amp; hardening&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as primary point of contact for ingestion and BigQuery platform incidents — freshness issues, schema drift, load failures — during business hours; this is not a formal on-call rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root-cause analysis for recurring ingestion/platform issues; convert findings into durable fixes and runbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain operational documentation — runbooks, escalation paths, and recovery procedures for the tools this role manages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core platform &amp;amp; tooling (must-have)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience with Google Cloud Platform, especially BigQuery, in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep enough BigQuery knowledge to advise others on best practices and evaluate new platform features for adoption, including cost optimisation (partitioning, clustering, slot management).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Dataplex — policy tags, taxonomies, PII/column-level masking, and fine-grained IAM roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GCP IAM, service accounts, and least-privilege access administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a regulated or PII-sensitive data environment (e.g. GDPR, HIPAA, or equivalent), given this role&#39;s direct exposure to sensitive-data controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ingestion &amp;amp; reliability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating or supporting an ELT ingestion tool such as Fivetran, Airbyte, or CData, with an eye for data integrity and pipeline performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monitoring, alerting, incident response, and root-cause analysis in a production data environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in data platform or cloud platform operations roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data fundamentals&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills; enough data-modelling fluency to troubleshoot across raw, staging, and mart layers without owning the modelling itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong documentation and runbook discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to use the GCP CLI and scripting (Python or Bash) to automate platform administration and access workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED EXPERIENCE (NICE-TO-HAVE)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with dbt — environments, scheduling, and access administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Tableau or a comparable BI platform — enough to recognise when a downstream issue traces back to a data source.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Salesforce, NetSuite, or other business-system data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a SaaS environment with high expectations for data freshness and business continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant Google Cloud certification (e.g. Professional Data Engineer, Professional Cloud Architect).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
